nymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033028 \"DB2 cell\")\n32815:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4033028 \"In primates, a diffuse bipolar 2 cell makes an average of 133 ribbon synapses, 47 contacts are with OFF parasol cells and 4 contacts are with OFF midget cells.\")\n32816:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033028 \"diffuse bipolar 2 cell\")\n32817:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033028 obo:CL_0000750)\n32819:# Class: obo:CL_4033029 (diffuse bipolar 3a cell)\n32821:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32555229\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33009001\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033029 \"An OFF calbindin-positive bipolar cell that has a large dendritic field and stratifies narrowly close to the middle of the inner plexiform layer. Its axon terminal is characterized by regularly branching and varicose processes resembling beads on a string. Most of DB3a contacts with cones are triad-associated.\")\n32822:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033029 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489>)\n32823:AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4033029 \"2023-04-04T10:53:33Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n32824:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.3389/fnana.2015.00122\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033029 \"DB3 cell\")\n32825:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033029 \"DB3a cell\")\n32826:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.3389/fnana.2015.00122\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4033029 \"Originally, DB3a cells were termed diffuse bipolar 3 (DB3) cells. When an additional bipolar type which stratifies slightly more vitread and is calbindin negative was detected, this cell was re