{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'rg -n \"database_cross_reference|hasDbXref .*http|hasDbXref .*https://\" src/ontology/cl-edit.owl'","aggregated_output":"3696:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"database_cross_reference\")\n3720:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdfs:seeAlso \"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso\")\n3828:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000005 \"Any fibroblast that is derived from the neural crest.\")\n3850:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ZFA:0007091\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000008 \"Cell that is part of the migratory cranial neural crest population. Migratory cranial neural crest cells develop from premigratory cranial neural crest cells and have undergone epithelial to mesenchymal transition and delamination.\")\n3873:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ZFA:0007095\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000011 \"Cell that is part of the migratory trunk neural crest population. Migratory trunk neural crest cells develop from premigratory trunk neural crest cells and have undergone epithelial to mesenchymal transition and delamination.\")\n3902:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29462262\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000015 \"A germ cell that supports male gamete production. In some species, non-germ cells known as Sertoli cells also play a role in spermatogenesis.\")\n4039:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000027 \"A smooth muscle cell derived from the neural crest.\")\n4069:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:NV\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neuroblast\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000031 \"A cell that will develop into a neuron often after a migration phase.\")\n4120:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19022770\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hematopoietic_stem_cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000037 \"A stem cell from which all cells of the lymphoid and myeloid lineages develop, including blood cells and cells of the immune system. Hematopoietic stem cells lack cell markers of effector cells (lin-negative). Lin-negative is defined by lacking one or more of the following cell surface markers: CD2, CD3 epsilon, CD4, CD5 ,CD8 alpha chain, CD11b, CD14, CD19, CD20, CD56, ly6G, ter119.\")\n4163:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:1104740\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monoblast\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.copewithcytokines.de\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000040 \"A myeloid progenitor cell committed to the monocyte lineage. This cell is CD11b-positive, has basophilic cytoplasm, euchromatin, and the presence of a nucleolus.\")\n4178:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.cap.org\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000041 \"A fully differentiated eosinophil, a granular leukocyte with a nucleus that usually has two lobes connected by one or more slender threads, and cytoplasm containing coarse, round granules that are uniform in size and which can be stained by the dye eosin. Cells are also differentiated from other granulocytes by a small nuclear-to-cytoplasm ratio (1:3). This cell type is CD49d-positive.\")\n4203:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18466030\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19231594\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20837449\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.cap.org\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000043 \"A fully differentiated basophil, a granular leukocyte with an irregularly shaped, pale-staining nucleus that is partially constricted into two lobes, and with cytoplasm that contains coarse granules of variable size. Basophils contain vasoactive amines such as histamine and serotonin, which are released on appropriate stimulation.\")\n4281:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D055015\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16647566\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Megakaryocyte-erythroid_progenitor_cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000050 \"A progenitor cell committed to the megakaryocyte and erythroid lineages.\")\n4362:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D005347\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fibroblast\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000057 \"A connective tissue cell which secretes an extracellular matrix rich in collagen and other macromolecules. Flattened and irregular in outline with branching processes; appear fusiform or spindle-shaped.\")\n4464:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"JB:jb\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34335193\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37008045\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9550134\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:/10.3389/fncel.2021.703951\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.britannica.com/science/ependymal-cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000065 \"A neuroepithelial glial cell, derived from a radial glial cell originating from the neuroectoderm, lines the ventricles of the brain and the central canal of the spinal cord. This cell is characterized by the presence of cilia on its apical surface, which can be motile or non-motile.\")\n4498:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000068 \"An epithelial cell that is part of a duct.\")\n4543:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO:0002065\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000075 \"A columnar/cuboidal epithelial cell is a cell usually found in a two dimensional sheet with a free surface. Columnar/cuboidal epithelial cells take on the shape of a column or cube.\")\n4573:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Epithelium\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:/10.1016/B978-0-12-410424-2.00003-2\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.biologyonline.com/dictionary/stratified-epithelium\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000079 \"An epithelial cell, organized into multiple layers, with only the basal layer being in contact with the basement membrane.\")\n4596:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000082 \"An epithelial cell of the lung.\")\n4720:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:amm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D006098\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Granulocyte\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000094 \"A leukocyte with abundant granules in the cytoplasm.\")\n4740:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D009504\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11138776\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12560239\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15514007\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:7880385\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.cap.org\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000096 \"A fully differentiated neutrophil, a granular leukocyte having a nucleus with three to five lobes connected by slender threads, and cytoplasm containing fine inconspicuous granules and stainable by neutral dyes. They are produced in bone marrow at a rate of 5e10-10e10/day and have a half-life of 6-8 hours. Neutrophils are CD15-positive, CD16-positive, CD32-positive, CD43-positive, CD181-positive, and CD182-positive.\")\n4931:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D042783\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21275341\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Endothelial_cell\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://sourceforge.net/tracker/?func=detail&atid=440764&aid=3364936&group_id=36855\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000115 \"An endothelial cell comprises the outermost layer or lining of anatomical structures and can be squamous or cuboidal. In mammals, endothelial cell has vimentin filaments and is derived from the mesoderm.\")\n4970:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1016/j.cnp.2022.11.002\") foaf:depiction obo:CL_0000119 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/CB_circuits_PMID3650468_f2.png>)\n4971:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.3389/fnins.2020.00293\") foaf:depiction obo:CL_0000119 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/Candelabrum_cell.png>)\n4979:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <https://medical-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/granule+cell>) obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000120 \"A neuron of the vertebrate central nervous system that is small in size. This general class includes small neurons in the granular layer of the cerebellar cortex, cerebral cortex neurons that are not pyramidal cells and small neurons without axons found in the olfactory bulb.\")\n4992:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.proghi.2004.07.002\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000121 \"cerebellar Purkinje cell\")\n4995:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17535929\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27215193\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37426070\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.stem.2023.11.013\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000121 \"Neurodegenerative disorders affecting Purkinje cells disrupt motor functions. Some of the neurodegenerative disorders that causes loss and degeration of Purkinje cells are Spinocerebellar ataxias (SCAs) (Josef P Kapfhammer and Etsuko Shimobayashi 2023), Friedreich's ataxia (FRDA) (Kevin C Kemp et al., 2016), Fetal alcohol syndrome (Laurent Servais et al., 2016), Dandy-Walker malformation (Alexander Atamian et al., 2024).\")\n4997:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1016/j.cnp.2022.11.002\") foaf:depiction obo:CL_0000121 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/CB_circuits_PMID3650468_f2.png>)\n4998:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.3389/fnins.2020.00293\") foaf:depiction obo:CL_0000121 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/Candelabrum_cell.jpg>)\n5051:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D001253\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11746784\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12162730\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12898703\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20942978\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Astrocyte\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000127 \"A class of large neuroglial (macroglial) cells in the central nervous system - the largest and most numerous neuroglial cells in the brain and spinal cord. Astrocytes (from 'star' cells) are irregularly shaped with many long processes, including those with 'end feet' which form the glial (limiting) membrane and directly and indirectly contribute to the blood-brain barrier. They regulate the extracellular ionic and chemical environment, and 'reactive astrocytes' (along with microglia) respond to injury.\")\n5062:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D009836\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oligodendrocyte\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000128 \"A class of large neuroglial (macroglial) cells in the central nervous system. Form the insulating myelin sheath of axons in the central nervous system.\")\n5077:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D017628\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11517395\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12430718\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14561199\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14612429\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16177057\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19461673\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:2089275\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microglia\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000129 \"A transcriptomically distinct central nervous system macrophage found in the parenchyma of the central nervous system. Marker include CD11b-positive, F4/80-positive, and CD68-positive.\")\n5083:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.copewithcytokines.de/\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000129 \"hortega cells\")\n5084:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.copewithcytokines.de/\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000129 \"microgliocyte\")\n5126:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"FB:ma\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMCID:PMC2613570\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:10102814\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16923606\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17986482\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19960544\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mesenchymal_stem_cell\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.copewithcytokines.de/cope.cgi?key=mesenchymal%20stem%20cells\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000134 \"A connective tissue cell that normally gives rise to other cells that are organized as three-dimensional masses. In humans, this cell type is CD73-positive, CD90-positive, CD105-positive, CD45-negative, CD34-negative, and MHCII-negative. They may further differentiate into osteoblasts, adipocytes, myocytes, neurons, or chondroblasts in vitro. Originally described as residing in the bone marrow, this cell type is now known to reside in many, if not all, adult organs.\")\n5381:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D020397\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goblet_cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000160 \"A specialized, columnar, mucus secreting epithelial cell shaped like a flask or goblet. A narrow basal end contains the nucleus while the apical end is swollen by the accumulation of mucus laden secretory granules.  Short microvilli project from the apical plasma membrane.\")\n5384:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000160 \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goblet_cell\")\n5387:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <http://cnx.org/content/col11496/1.6/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=30131227>) foaf:depiction obo:CL_0000160 \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/404_Goblet_Cell_new.jpg/800px-404_Goblet_Cell_new.jpg\")\n5442:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:5342440\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.clinicalkey.com/#!/content/book/3-s2.0-B9780323555968000073\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000165 \"The neurosecretory cell is neither an ordinary neuron nor an endocrine cell, but a combination of both. Its neuronal features resemble those of ordinary neurons concerning both structure and function. The production of a visible secretory material marks the neurosecretory neuron as a gland cell, and the fact that extractable cellular products act in the manner of hormones places it in the realm of endocrine elements. \n5475:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pancreatic_b_cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000169 \"A cell that secretes insulin and is located towards the center of the islets of Langerhans.\")\n5591:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000180 \"A steroid hormone secreting cell that secretes estradiol.\")\n5605:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0412046911\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D022781\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19717280\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hepatocyte\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000182 \"The main structural component of the liver. They are specialized epithelial cells that are organized into interconnected plates called lobules. Majority of cell population of liver, polygonal in shape, arranged in plates or trabeculae between sinusoids; may have single nucleus or binucleated.\")\n5701:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D032389\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9315361\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smooth_muscle_cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000192 \"A non-striated, elongated, spindle-shaped cell found lining the digestive tract, uterus, and blood vessels. They develop from specialized myoblasts (smooth muscle myoblast).\")\n6036:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D001792\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11110672\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16987572\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17204662\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17479180\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20414831\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Platelet\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000233 \"A non-nucleated disk-shaped cell formed by extrusion from megakaryocytes, found in the blood of all mammals, and mainly involved in blood coagulation.\")\n6112:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000239 <https://doi.org/10.1152/ajpgi.00005.2011>)\n6799:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.britannica.com/EBchecked/topic/6405/adrenal-gland\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000336 \"A cell found within the adrenal medulla that secrete biogenic amine hormones upon stimulation.\")\n7226:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.1016/B978-012369493-5.50008-0\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000394 \"A phagocytic hemocyte, responsible for the engulfment of small particles, microbes, and apoptotic tissue debris. It may also secretes antimicrobial peptides and contribute to the production and secretion of proteins of the hemolymph.\")\n7342:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.wormatlas.org/hermaphrodite/hypodermis/mainframe.htm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000411 \"An epithelial cell of the hypodermis of Caenorhabditis.\")\n7353:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"FB:ma\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32646579\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://bio.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Introductory_and_General_Biology/Biology_(Kimball)/07%3A_Cell_Division/7.04%3A_Polyploidy\"^^xsd:anyURI) obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000412 \"A cell that contains more than two haploid sets of chromosomes.\")\n7393:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.wormatlas.org/ver1/handbook/hypodermis/hypsupportother.htm#arcadecells\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000418 \"An epithelial cell found in C. elegans that firmly hold the outer body wall and the lips to the inner cylinder of the pharynx in a manner that keeps these organs from breaking apart, while still giving each organ freedom of movement during feeding.\")\n7401:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.wormatlas.org/hermaphrodite/seam%20cells/mainframe.htm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000419 \"An epithelial fate stem cell found in flatworms.\")\n7457:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://wormatlas.psc.edu/hermaphrodite/muscleGLR/mainframe.htm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000427 \"A scaffolding cell type found in C. elegans, this cell plays a supportive role to the muscle arms. May also have an endocrine role.\")\n7494:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reticular_cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000432 \"A fibroblast that synthesizes collagen and uses it to produce reticular fibers, thus providing structural support. Reticular cells are found in many organs, including the spleen, lymph nodes and kidneys. Subtypes of reticular cells include epithelial, mesenchymal, and fibroblastic reticular cells. Fibroblastic reticular cells are involved in directing B cells and T cells to specific regions within a tissue, whereas epithelial and mesenchymal reticular cells are associated with certain areas of the brain.\")\n7528:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gonadotroph\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000437 \"A rounded cell that is usually situated next to sinusoids; secretes follicular stimulating hormone (FSH) and luteinizing hormone (LH).\")\n7901:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000483 \"A peptide hormone secreting cell that secretes bombesin stimulating hormone.\")\n7939:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:bf\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11171397\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:24397521\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34208190\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/oenocyte\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000487 \"A secretory cell of ectodermal origin. This cell may have important functions in fatty acid and hydrocarbon metabolism and is metabolically linked to the fat body and tracheae. This cell is exclusive of arthropods.\")\n8018:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Interneuron\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000498 \"An interneuron (also called relay neuron, association neuron or local circuit neuron) is a multipolar neuron which connects afferent neurons and efferent neurons in neural pathways. Like motor neurons, interneuron cell bodies are always located in the central nervous system (CNS).\")\n8349:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D009474\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neuron\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000540 \"The basic cellular unit of nervous tissue. Each neuron consists of a body, an axon, and dendrites. Their purpose is to receive, conduct, and transmit impulses in the nervous system.\")\n8548:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D008533\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31043076\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Megakaryocyte\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000556 \"A large hematopoietic cell (50 to 100 micron) with a lobated nucleus. Once mature, this cell undergoes multiple rounds of endomitosis and cytoplasmic restructuring to allow platelet formation and release.\")\n8564:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:amm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D055014\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMCID:PMC2213186\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMCID:PMC548021\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16551251\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16647566\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CFU-GM\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.copewithcytokines.de\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000557 \"A hematopoietic progenitor cell that is committed to the granulocyte and monocyte lineages. These cells are CD123-positive, and do not express Gata1 or Gata2 but do express C/EBPa, and Pu.1.\")\n8565:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.copewithcytokines.de\") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_0000557 \"CFU-C , Colony forming unit in culture\")\n8602:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:10618520\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12560239\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15514007\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.cap.org\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000560 \"A late neutrophilic metamyelocyte in which the nucleus is indented to more than half the distance to the farthest nuclear margin but in no area being condensed to a single filament. The nucleus is in the form of a curved or coiled band, not having acquired the typical multilobar shape of the mature neutrophil. These cells are fMLP receptor-positive, CD11b-positive, CD35-negative, and CD49d-negative.\")\n8800:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:10618520\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12560239\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15514007\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.cap.org\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000580 \"A neutrophil precursor in the granulocytic series, being a cell intermediate in development between a promyelocyte and a metamyelocyte; in this stage, production of primary granules is complete and neutrophil-specific granules has started. No nucleolus is present. This cell type is CD13-positive, CD16-negative, integrin alpha-M-positive, CD15-positive, CD33-positive, CD24-positive, C/EBP-a-positive, C/EBPe-positive, PU.1-positive, lactotransferrin-positive, myeloperoxidase-positive and NGAL-positive.\")\n8822:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:10618520\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12560239\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15514007\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.cap.org\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000582 \"A neutrophil precursor in the granulocytic series, being a cell intermediate in development between a myelocyte and the band form neutrophil. The protein synthesis seen in earlier stages decreases or stops; the nucleus becomes indented where the indentation is smaller than half the distance to the farthest nuclear margin; chromatin becomes coarse and clumped; specific granules predominate while primary granules are rare; and the cytoplasm becomes amphophilic like that of a mature granulocyte. This cell type is integrin alpha-M-positive, CD13-negative, CD15-positive, CD16-positive, CD33-positive, CD24-positive, fMLP receptor-negative and has expression of C/EBP-a, C/EBP-e, PU.1 transcription factor, lactotransferrin, myeloperoxidase and neutrophil gelatinase associated lipocalin.\")\n8852:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33290721\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9610-7627\") oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:CL_0000584 \"differentiated enterocyte\")\n8853:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33290721\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9610-7627\") oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:CL_0000584 \"mature enterocyte\")\n8915:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000591 \"A thermoreceptor cell that detects increased temperatures.\")\n9089:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19622087\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.cap.org\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000612 \"A eosinophil precursor in the granulocytic series, being a cell intermediate in development between a promyelocyte and a metamyelocyte;in this stage, production of primary granules is complete and eosinophil-specific granules has started. No nucleolus is present. These cells are integrin alpha-M-positive, CD13-positive, CD15-positive, CD16-negative, CD24-positive, and CD33-positive.\")\n9099:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMCID:PMC1312421\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.copewithcytokines.de\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000613 \"A progenitor cell committed to the basophil lineage. This cell lacks hematopoietic lineage markers (lin-negative) and is CD34-positive, T1/ST2-low, CD117-negative, and FceRIa-high. This cell also expresses Gata-1, Gata-2 and C/EBPa.\")\n9112:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18466030\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.cap.org\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000614 \"A basophil precursor in the granulocytic series, being a cell intermediate in development between a promyelocyte and a metamyelocyte; in this stage, production of primary granules is complete and basophil-specific granules has started. No nucleolus is present. Markers are being integrin alpha-M-positive, fucosyltransferase FUT4-positive, CD33-positive, CD24-positive, aminopeptidase N-positive.\")\n9172:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.copewithcytokines.de\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000622 \"A secretory cell that is grouped together with other cells of the same type to form grape shaped clusters known as acini (singular acinus).\")\n9270:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D055166\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12808230\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17239632\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18222966\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9302568\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hepatic_stellate_cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000632 \"A cell that is found in the perisinusoidal space of the liver that is capable of multiple roles including storage of retinol, presentation of antigen to T cells (including CD1d-restricted NKT cells), and upon activation, production of extracellular matrix components that can contribute to liver fibrosis. This activated state has a myofibroblast-like phenotype, though it's not clear in the literature if this is terminally differentiated. This cell type comprises approximately 8-15% of total cells in the liver.\")\n9309:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721662544\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.britannica.com/EBchecked/topic/156177/Deiters-cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000635 \"The outer phalangeal cells of the organ of Corti. This cell holds the base of the hair cell in a cup-shaped depression.\")\n9394:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.neurolex.org/wiki/Category:Bergmann_Glial_Cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000644 \"Type of radial astrocyte in the cerebellar cortex that have their cell bodies in the Purkinje cell layer and processes that extend into the molecular layer, terminating with bulbous endfeet at the pial surface. Bergmann glia express high densities of glutamate transporters that limit diffusion of the neurotransmitter glutamate during its release from synaptic terminals. Besides their role in early development of the cerebellum, Bergmann glia are also required for the pruning or addition of synapses.\")\n9399:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.3389/fnins.2020.00293\") foaf:depiction obo:CL_0000644 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/Candelabrum_cell.jpg>)\n9405:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0412046911\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31915267\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pituicyte\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000645 \"A glial cell of astrocytic lineage with long processes running parallel to adjacent axons in the proximal infundibulum of the neurohypophysis. These processes form a three-dimensional network among the axons of the hypothalamic neurosecretory cells and are connected by gap junctions which provide for their metabolic coupling. This cell type constitutes most of the nonexcitable tissue in the neurohypophsis; function may include possibly acting as an intermediate in the modulation of oxytocin and vasopressin release. This cell type is highly variable in size and shape and commonly contain lipid droplets and deposits of lipochrome pigment.\")\n9463:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.copewithcytokines.de/cope.cgi?key=mesangial%20cells\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000650 \"A cell type that encapsulates the capillaries and venules in the kidney. This cell secretes mesangial matrix that provides the structural support for the capillaries.\")\n9486:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16687276\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pinealocyte\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000652 \"This cell type produces and secretes melatonin and forms the pineal parenchyma. Extending from each cell body, which has a spherical, oval or lobulated mucleus, are one or more tortuous basophilic processes, containing parallel microtubules known as synaptic ribbons. These processes end in expanded terminal buds near capillaries or less, frequently, ependymal cells of the pineal recess. The terminal buds contain granular endoplasmic reticulum, mitochondria and electron-dense cored vesicles, which store monoamines and polypeptide hormones, release of which appears to require sympathetic innervation.\")\n9497:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.1101/2021.10.10.463829\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000653 \"A specialized kidney epithelial cell, contained within a glomerulus, that contains \\\"feet\\\" that interdigitate with the \\\"feet\\\" of other podocytes.\")\n9754:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"JB:jb\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://neurolex.org/wiki/Category:Ependymoglial_Cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000683 \"A cell that transports hormones from neurosecretory cells. This nerve cell is characterized by bipolar shape and endfeet that contact a basal lamina around blood vessels, and/or the pia mater or vitreous body of the eye and additionally contact the ventricular surface or sub-retinal space.\")\n9979:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.copewithcytokines.org/cope.cgi?key=cumulus%20cells\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000711 \"Cumulus cell is a specialized granulosa cell that surrounds and nourishes the oocyte. This cell-type surrounds the fully-grown oocyte to form a cumulus-oocyte complex (abbr. COC). The terms cumulus oophorus cells, cumulus granulosa cells, cumulus oophorous granulosa cells, granulosa-cumulus cells are used to make a distinction between this cell and the other functionally different subpopulation of granulosa cells at the wall of the Graafian follicle.\")\n10485:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18466030\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.cap.org\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000770 \"A late basophilic metamyelocyte in which the nucleus is in the form of a curved or coiled band, not having acquired the typical multilobar shape of the mature basophil.\")\n10531:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19622087\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.cap.org\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000774 \"A late eosinophilic metamyelocyte in which the nucleus is in the form of a curved or coiled band, not having acquired the typical multilobar shape of the mature eosinophil.\")\n10674:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0781735149\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19447676\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20081059\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20839338\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20951740\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plasma_cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000786 \"A terminally differentiated, post-mitotic, antibody secreting cell of the B cell lineage with the phenotype CD138-positive, surface immunonoglobulin-negative, and MHC Class II-negative. Plasma cells are oval or round with extensive rough endoplasmic reticulum, a well-developed Golgi apparatus, and a round nucleus having a characteristic cartwheel heterochromatin pattern and are devoted to producing large amounts of immunoglobulin.\")\n10692:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:rhs\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0781735149\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20081059\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20839338\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Memory_B_cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000787 \"A memory B cell is a mature B cell that is long-lived, readily activated upon re-encounter of its antigenic determinant, and has been selected for expression of higher affinity immunoglobulin. This cell type has the phenotype CD19-positive, CD20-positive, MHC Class II-positive, and CD138-negative.\")\n10919:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0781735149\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.immgen.org/index_content.html\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000805 \"A thymocyte that has the phenotype CD4-negative, CD8-positive, CD44-negative, CD25-negative, and pre-TCR-positive.\")\n11115:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11861604\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20933013\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21220451\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/B-1_cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000819 \"A B cell of distinct lineage and surface marker expression. B-1 B cells are thought to be the primary source of natural IgM immunoglobulin, that is, IgM produced in large quantities without prior antigenic stimulation and generally reactive against various microorganisms, as well as the source of T-independent IgA immunoglobulin in the mucosal areas. These cells are CD43-positive.\")\n11277:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMCID:PMC1183570\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMCID:PMC1312421\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:8629001\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9354811\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.copewithcytokines.de\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000831 \"A progenitor cell of the mast cell lineage. Markers for this cell are FceRIa-low, CD117-positive, CD9-positive, T1/ST2-positive, SCA1-negative, and lineage-negative.\")\n11316:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Myeloblast\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.cap.org\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000835 \"The most primitive precursor in the granulocytic series, having fine, evenly distributed chromatin, several nucleoli, a high nuclear-to-cytoplasmic ration (5:1-7:1), and a nongranular basophilic cytoplasm. They reside in the bone marrow.\")\n11326:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:amm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.cap.org\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000836 \"A precursor in the granulocytic series, being a cell intermediate in development between a myeloblast and myelocyte, that has distinct nucleoli, a nuclear-to-cytoplasmic ratio of 5:1 to 3:1, and containing a few primary cytoplasmic granules. Markers for this cell are fucosyltransferase FUT4-positive, CD33-positive, integrin alpha-M-negative, low affinity immunoglobulin gamma Fc region receptor III-negative, and CD24-negative.\")\n11408:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0781735149\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMCID:PMC2193793\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20933013\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Follicular_B_Cells\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000843 \"A resting mature B cell that has the phenotype IgM-positive, IgD-positive, CD23-positive and CD21-positive, and found in the B cell follicles of the white pulp of the spleen or the corticol areas of the peripheral lymph nodes. This cell type is also described as being CD19-positive, B220-positive, AA4-negative, CD43-negative, and CD5-negative.\")\n11437:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0781735149\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:10933592\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20933013\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marginal-zone_B_cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000845 \"A mature B cell that is located in the marginal zone of the spleen with the phenotype CD23-negative and CD21-positive and expressing a B cell receptor usually reactive to bacterial cell wall components or senescent self components such as oxidized-LDL. This cell type is also described as being CD19-positive, B220-positive, IgM-high, AA4-negative, CD35-high.\")\n11620:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:ana\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2825-0621\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000865 \"A gut-associated lymphoid tissue macrophage found in lamina propria of the gut.\")\n11877:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19100699\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22343568\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.immgen.org/index_content.html\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000895 \"An antigen inexperienced CD4-positive, alpha-beta T cell with the phenotype CCR7-positive, CD127-positive and CD62L-positive. This cell type develops in the thymus. This cell type is also described as being CD25-negative, CD62L-high, and CD44-low.\")\n11903:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0781735149\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.immgen.org/index_content.html\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000897 \"A CD4-positive, alpha-beta T cell that has differentiated into a memory T cell.\")\n11945:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0781735149\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22343568\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.immgen.org/index_content.html\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000900 \"A CD8-positive, alpha-beta T cell that has not experienced activation via antigen contact and has the phenotype CD45RA-positive, CCR7-positive and CD127-positive. This cell type is also described as being CD25-negative, CD62L-high and CD44-low.\")\n12669:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:msz\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12810111\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17174121\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.immgen.org/index_content.html\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000960 \"A transitional stage B cell that expresses surface IgM and IgD, and CD62L. This cell type appears to be an anergic B cell that does not proliferate upon BCR signaling, is found in the spleen and lymph nodes, and has the phenotype surface IgM-positive, surface IgD-positive, CD21-positive, CD23-positive, CD62L-positive, and CD93-positive. This cell type has also been described as IgM-low, CD19-positive, B220-positive, AA4-positive, and CD23-positive (i.e. this cell-type is distinguished from T2 cells by surface expression of IgM).\")\n13071:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:amm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMCID:PMC2346585\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.immgen.org/index_content.html\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000998 \"CD8-alpha-negative CD11b-negative dendritic cell is a conventional dendritic cell that is CD11b-negative, CD4-negative CD8-alpha-negative and is CD205-positive. This cell is able to cross- present antigen to CD8-alpha-positive T cells.\")\n13299:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:amm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:1261582\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17952047\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.immgen.org/index_content.html\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0001023 \"A common myeloid progenitor that is Kit-positive and CD34-positive, Il7ra-negative, and is SCA1-low and Fcgr2-low and Fcgr3-low.\")\n13320:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:amm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17952047\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.immgen.org/index_content.html\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0001025 \"A common lymphoid progenitor that is Kit-low, FLT3-positive, IL7ralpha-positive, and SCA1-low.\")\n13386:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1016/j.cnp.2022.11.002\") foaf:depiction obo:CL_0001031 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/CB_circuits_PMID3650468_f2.png>)\n13387:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.3389/fnins.2020.00293\") foaf:depiction obo:CL_0001031 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/Candelabrum_cell.jpg>)\n13678:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0001061 \"https://ncit.nci.nih.gov/ncitbrowser/ConceptReport.jsp?dictionary=NCI_Thesaurus&code=C12913\")\n13702:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0001063 \"https://ncit.nci.nih.gov/ncitbrowser/ConceptReport.jsp?dictionary=NCI_Thesaurus&code=C12922\")\n13715:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0001064 \"https://ncit.nci.nih.gov/ncitbrowser/ConceptReport.jsp?dictionary=NCI_Thesaurus&code=C12917\")\n13934:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0781735149\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21926977\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:24258910\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.immgen.org/index_content.html\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0001204 \"CD4-positive, alpha-beta long-lived T cell with the phenotype CD45RO-positive and CD127-positive. This cell type is also described as being CD25-negative.\")\n13951:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:ak\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19805084\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.immgen.org/index_content.html\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002000 \"An erythroid progenitor cell is Kit-positive, Ly6A-negative, CD41-negative, CD127-negative, and CD123-negative. This cell type is also described as being lin-negative, Kit-positive, CD150-negative, CD41-negative, CD105-positive, and FcgR-negative.\")\n13974:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12615892\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16322423\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19022770\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19273628\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.immgen.org/index_content.html\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002002 \"A granulocyte monocyte progenitor that is Kit-positive, CD34-positive, Fc-gamma receptor II/II-positive, and is Sca-1-negative, Il7ra-negative, Cxc3r1-negative, and CD90-negative.\")\n14018:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12615892\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19022770\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.immgen.org/index_content.html\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002006 \"A megakaryocyte erythroid progenitor cell that is Kit-positive and is Sca1-negative, CD34-negative, CD90-negative, IL7r-alpha-negative and Fcgr II/III-low.\")\n14303:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19022770\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002032 \"A hematopoietic oligopotent progenitor cell that has the ability to differentiate into limited cell types but lacks lineage cell markers and self renewal capabilities.\")\n14403:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16087715\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17589542\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19423665\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26802287\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:38440725\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.immgen.org/index_content.html\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002040 \"A CD24-low, CD44-negative, NK1.1-negative NK T cell.\")\n14427:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16087715\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17589542\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19423665\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26802287\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:38440725\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.immgen.org/index_content.html\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002042 \"A CD24-low, CD44-positive, DX5-high, NK1.1-negative NK T cell.\")\n14460:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:ak\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12633665\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17582343\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37442242\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.immgen.org/index_content.html\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002045 \"A pro-B cell that is CD45R/B220-positive, CD43-positive, HSA-low, BP-1-negative and Ly6c-negative. This cell type is also described as being lin-negative, AA4-positive, Kit-positive, IL7Ra-positive and CD45R-positive.\")\n14541:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:ak\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17582343\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18432934\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37442242\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.immgen.org/index_content.html\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002052 \"A pre-B cell that is pre-BCR-negative, and the kappa- and lambda- light immunoglobulin light chain-negative, CD43-low, and is BP-1-positive, CD45R-positive and CD25-positive. This cell type is also described as being AA4-positive, IgM-negative, CD19-positive, CD43-low/negative, and HSA-positive.\")\n14621:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19273629\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.immgen.org/index_content.html\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002059 \"A conventional thymic dendritic cell that is CD8-alpha-positive.\")\n14653:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20054144\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29463737\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.copewithcytokines.de\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002062 \"A squamous pulmonary alveolar epithelial cell that is flattened and branched. A pulmonary alveolar type 1 cell covers more than 98% of the alveolar surface. This large cell has thin (50-100 nm) cytoplasmic extensions to form the air-blood barrier essential for normal gas exchange.\")\n14677:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0412046911\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36138472\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:8540632\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.copewithcytokines.de\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002063 \"A pulmonary alveolar epithelial cell that modulates the fluid surrounding the alveolar epithelium by secreting and recycling surfactants via specialized organelles called alveolar lamellar bodies. This cell type also contributes to tissue repair and can differentiate after injury into a pulmonary alveolar type 1 cell. This cuboidal cell is thicker than squamous alveolar cells, has a rounded apical surface that projects above the level of the surrounding epithelium, and its free surface is covered by short microvilli.\")\n14703:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20395539\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.copewithcytokines.de/cope.cgi?key=pancreatic%20acinar%20cells\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002064 \"A secretory cell found in pancreatic acini that secretes digestive enzymes and mucins. This cell is a typical zymogenic cell, have a basal nucleus and basophilic cytoplasm consisting of regular arrays of granular endoplasmic reticulum with mitochondria and dense secretory granules.\")\n14892:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:7938227\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carotid_body\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002081 \"This cell resembles a glia cell, express the glial marker S100 and act as a supporting cell to type I cell. This cell is located in a small cluster of type I and type II cells near the fork of the carotid artery.\")\n14927:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boettcher_cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002084 \"A Boettcher cell is a polyhedral cells on the basilar membrane of the cochlea, and is located beneath Claudius cells. A Boettcher cell is considered a supporting cell for the organ of Corti, and is present only in the lower turn of the cochlea. These cells interweave with each other, and project microvilli into the intercellular space. Because of their structural specialization, a Boettcher cell is believed to play a significant role in the function of the cochlea. They demonstrate high levels of calmodulin, and may be involved in mediating Ca(2+) regulation and ion transport.\")\n14938:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29351662\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://neurolex.org/wiki/Category:Tanycyte\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002085 \"A specialized elongated ventricular ependymal cell with one or more processes that extend into the brain parenchyma or associated blood vessels where they contact blood vessel endothelial cells and/or neurons. These cells are found in the ventricles and circumventricular organs of the brain. They are involved in hormonal regulation, gatekeeping molecules between the bloodstream and cerebrospinal fluid, metabolic sensing, and regulating food intake.\")\n14995:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:068340007X\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polar_body\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002090 \"One of two small cells formed by the first and second meiotic division of oocytes.\")\n15609:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <https://doi.org/10.1016/B978-032304048-8.50071-2>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25386990\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0002145 \"These cells possess numerous cilia on their surface, typically ranging from 200 to 300 per cell. The cilia vary in length, measuring between 6 to 7 μm in the upper airways (trachea) and becoming shorter, around 4 μm, in the smaller airways (terminal bronchioles). These cells form a two-layered 'coat' in the airway: the lower 'sol' layer is watery, allowing the cilia to beat in coordinated waves, while the upper 'gel' layer is thick and sticky, trapping inhaled particles.\")\n15780:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.theodora.com/anatomy/the_internal_ear_or_labyrinth.html\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002163 \"A rod-shpaed cell that forms a single row adjacent to and supporting the inner hair cells.\")\n15789:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.theodora.com/anatomy/the_internal_ear_or_labyrinth.html\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002164 \"A rod-shaped cell found in 3 or 4 rows that lie adjacent to and support the outer hair cells.\")\n15883:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0412046911\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http:/www.copewithcytokines.de/cope.cgi?key=Lacis%20cells\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002173 \"A cell that is a specialized type of pericyte providing structural support for the capillary loops of kidney. A flat, elongated cell with extensive fine cytoplasmic processes found outside the kidney glomerulus near the macula densa and bound laterally by afferent and efferent arterioles. Being phagocytic, this cell participates in the continuous turnover of the basal lamina by removing its outer portion containing residues of filtration, while the lamina is renewed on its inner surface by the endothelial cells.\")\n16093:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metamyelocyte\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002192 \"A eosinophil precursor in the granulocytic series, being a cell intermediate in development between a myelocyte and a band form cell. The nucleus becomes indented where the indentation is smaller than half the distance to the farthest nuclear margin; chromatin becomes coarse and clumped; specific granules predominate while primary granules are rare.\")\n16103:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0323052908\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Myelocyte\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002193 \"A cell type that is the first of the maturation stages of the granulocytic leukocytes normally found in the bone marrow. Granules are seen in the cytoplasm. The nuclear material of the myelocyte is denser than that of the myeloblast but lacks a definable membrane. The cell is flat and contains increasing numbers of granules as maturation progresses.\")\n16137:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <https://doi.org/10.1038/s12276-020-0483-0>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <https://doi.org/10.3389/fcell.2021.644088>) obo:RO_0004050 obo:CL_0002196 \"Liver progenitor cells have been variously named in rodent and human studies as oval cells, hepatic progenitor cells, liver stem cells, ductular reactions, or atypical ductular cells. They were first described as oval cells in rats due to their large nuclear-to-cytoplasm ratio and oval-shaped nuclei. On the difference between 'hepatic liver stem cells' (HLSC) and 'oval cells':  \\\"... unlike a well-known hepatic progenitor cell population, known as oval cells in rodents, HLSCs do not express CK-7, CK-19, c-kit, CD133 and alpha-smooth muscle actin (α-SMA) (Gaudio et al., 2009)\\\".\")\n16143:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(terms:contributor <http://orcid.org/0000-0003-1940-6740>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <https://doi.org/10.1038/s12276-020-0483-0>) oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0002196 \"hepatic progenitor cell\")\n16144:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <https://doi.org/10.1038/s12276-020-0483-0>) oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0002196 \"liver progenitor cell\")\n16215:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-4183-8865\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0002203 \"brush cell of large intestine\")\n16216:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-4183-8865\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0002203 \"tuft cell of epithelium of large intestine\")\n16354:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skeletal_muscle\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002215 \"A type II muscle cell that contains a low content of myoglobin, relatively few mitochondria, relatively few blood capillaries and large amounts of glycogen. Type II B fibres are white, geared to generate ATP by anaerobic metabolic processes, not able to supply skeletal muscle fibres continuously with sufficient ATP, fatigue easily, split ATP at a fast rate and have a fast contraction velocity.\")\n16376:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.med.yale.edu/obgyn/kliman/placenta/articles/EOR_Placenta/Trophtoplacenta.html\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002217 \"A trophoblast that leaves the placenta and invades the endometrium and myometrium. This cell type is crucial in increasing blood flow to the fetus.\")\n16386:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.immgen.org\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002218 \"A double negative thymocyte that has a T cell receptor consisting of a gamma chain that has as part a Vgamma3 segment, and a delta chain. This cell type is CD4-negative, CD8-negative and CD24-positive. This cell-type is found in the fetal thymus with highest numbers occurring at E17-E18.\")\n16397:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.med.yale.edu/obgyn/kliman/placenta/articles/EOR_Placenta/Trophtoplacenta.html\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002219 \"A trophoblast found at the junction of the placenta. This cell type makes a unique fibronectin-trophouteronectin junction that helps mediate attachment of the placenta to the uterus. This cell type is also found junction of the chorion layer of the external membranes and the decidua.\")\n16447:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721662544\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lens_%28anatomy%29#Lens_epithelium\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002224 \"A cell of the cuboidal epithelium that covers the lens. The cells of the lens epithelium regulate most of the homeostatic functions of the lens. As ions, nutrients, and liquid enter the lens from the aqueous humor, Na+/K+ ATPase pumps in the lens epithelial cells pump ions out of the lens to maintain appropriate lens osmolarity and volume, with equatorially positioned lens epithelium cells contributing most to this current. The activity of the Na+/K+ ATPases keeps water and current flowing through the lens from the poles and exiting through the equatorial regions. The cells of the lens epithelium also serve as the progenitors for new lens fibers. It constantly lays down fibers in the embryo, fetus, infant, and adult, and continues to lay down fibers for lifelong growth.\")\n16662:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32644501\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:/10.1016/j.autneu.2015.04.008\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.bu.edu/histology/p/19404loa.htm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002244 \"A stratified squamous epithelial cell located in the ectocervix.\")\n16777:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11331626\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30013421\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30309298\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31907034\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Decidualization\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41591-020-1040-z\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002255 \"A stromal cell of the endometrium, characterized by its fibroblast-like morphology, regenerative capacity, and ability to undergo decidualization. It differentiates into a decidual stromal cell during pregnancy, essential for embryo implantation and maintenance. This cell is involved in tissue proliferation, remodeling, and breakdown, responding to hormonal changes, particularly estrogen and progesterone.\")\n16792:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:8985136\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.copewithcytokines.de/cope.cgi?key=glomus%20cells\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002256 \"A supportive cell that has characteristics of glial cell. Processes of this cell envelope the junctions between glomus cells and nerve endings.\")\n17306:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34433485\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fibroblast-like_synoviocyte\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0002301 \"Type B synovial cells play a key role in the pathogenesis of chronic inflammatory diseases, such as rheumatoid arthritis, and are essential for the maintenance of normal joint functions. Fibroblast-like synoviocytes from different joints have different properties, which may contribute to the characteristic pattern of joint involvement in different types of arthritis.\")\n17334:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.exer.2003.09.021\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0002303 \"PE cell\")\n17335:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.exer.2003.09.021\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0002303 \"In a consensus model of unidirectional secretion, aqueous humour is formed by transferring solute, principally NaCl, from stroma to posterior chamber, with water passively following the osmotic gradient. Unidirectional secretion comprises three sequential steps. First, NaCl is transferred from the stromal interstitium into the pigmented ciliary epithelial (PE) cells. Second, solute passes from the PE into the non-pigmented ciliary epithelial (NPE) cells through gap junctions. Finally, NPE cells release Na+ and Cl− into the aqueous humour.\")\n17346:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.exer.2003.09.021\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0002304 \"NPE cell\")\n17348:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.exer.2003.09.021\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0002304 \"In a consensus model of unidirectional secretion, aqueous humour is formed by transferring solute, principally NaCl, from stroma to posterior chamber, with water passively following the osmotic gradient. Unidirectional secretion comprises three sequential steps. First, NaCl is transferred from the stromal interstitium into the pigmented ciliary epithelial (PE) cells. Second, solute passes from the PE into the non-pigmented ciliary epithelial (NPE) cells through gap junctions. Finally, NPE cells release Na+ and Cl− into the aqueous humour.\")\n17795:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19949422\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http:www.immgen.org/index_content.html\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002345 \"An immature natural killer cell that is NK1.1-positive, DX5-positive, Ly49-positive, CD27-low and CD11b-low. This cell type is found in high numbers in the liver.\")\n18142:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.immgen.org\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002378 \"A double negative thymocyte that has a T cell receptor consisting of a gamma chain containing a Vgamma2 segment, and a delta chain. This cell type is CD4-negative, CD8-negative and CD24-positive and is found in the fetal thymus.\")\n18152: