o locations.\")\n22622:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:CVS\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18356246\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20483998\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26798363\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1940-6740\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0005026 \"Multi fate stem cell that gives rise to both hepatocytes and cholangiocytes as descendants. The term often refers to fetal precursors of hepatocytes (differently from 'hepatic stem cell', usually applied to the self-renewing pool of hepatocyte precursors in the adult liver). Hepatoblasts may also be endogenous, as some stem cells found in the liver come from the bone marrow via blood circulation.\")\n22837:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/583\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0007021 \"club cell (zebrafish)\")\n22838:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN-10:0412429403\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/583\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0007021 \"club cell\")\n23176:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7073-9172\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0008041 \"A mesothelial cell that is part of the intestinal serosa.\")\n23317:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0009002 \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inflammatory_response\")\n23326:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0009003 \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Insect#Midgut\")\n23346:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0009005 \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salivary_gland\")\n23353:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009006 \"An enteroendocrine cell that is located in the small intestine.\")\n23367:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4183-8865\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009007 \"A macrophage which is resident in the lamina propria of the small intestine.\")\n23377:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4183-8865\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009008 \"A macrophage which is resident in the lamina propria of the large intestine.\")\n23387:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31753849\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-4183-8865\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009009 \"A paneth cell that is located in the epithelium of the colon.\")\n23399:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:24813615\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28835754\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-4183-8865\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009010 \"Transit-amplifying cells (TACs) are an undifferentiated population in transition between stem cells and differentiated cells.\")\n23412:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20801415\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-4183-8865\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009011 \"A rapidly proliferating population of cells that differentiate from stem cells of the intestinal crypt of the colon. Stem cells located in the crypts of Lieberkühn give rise to proliferating progenitor or transit amplifying cells that differentiate into the four major epithelial cell types. These include columnar absorptive cells or enterocytes, mucous secreting goblet cells, enteroendocrine cells and paneth cells.\")\n23427:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20801415\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-4183-8865\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009012 \"A rapidly proliferating population of cells that differentiate from stem cells of the intestinal crypt of the small intestine. Stem cells located in the crypts of Lieberkühn give rise to proliferating progenitor or transit amplifying cells that differentiate into the four major epithelial cell types. These include columnar absorptive cells or enterocytes, mucous secreting goblet cells, enteroendocrine cells and paneth cells.\")\n23445:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31350390\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3163-0115\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009013 \"A progenitor cell with hepatic and biliary lineage potential, identified in mouse and human, and anatomically restricted to the ductal plate of fetal liver.\")\n23457:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23525039\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9252325\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4183-8865\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009014 \"A lymphocyte that is part of a Peyer's patch. These cells have a major role in driving the immune response to antigens sampled from the intestinal lumen, and in regulating the formation of follicle-associated epithelium and M cells in Peyer's patches by converting intestitial enterocytes into M cells.\")\n23467:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:24437401\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4183-8865\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009015 \"A follicular dendritic cell located in the Peyer's patch. These cells from a meshwork in which Peyer's patch B cells reside.\")\n23475:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20683682\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4183-8865\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009016 \"An intestinal stem cell that is located in the large intestine crypt of Liberkuhn. These stem cells reside at the bottom of crypts in the large intestine and are highly proliferative. They either differentiate into transit amplifying cells or self-renew to form new stem cells.\")\n23485:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20683682\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4183-8865\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009017 \"An intestinal stem cell that is located in the small intestine crypt of Liberkuhn. These stem cells reside at the bottom of crypts in the small intestine and are highly proliferative. They either differentiate into transit amplifying cells or self-renew to form new stem cells.\")\n23499:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4183-8865\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009018 \"A lymphocyte that resides in the lamina propria of the large intestine.\")\n23509:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29449449\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3163-0115\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009019 \"A kidney cortical cell that is part of the nephrogenic zone.\")\n23519:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009020 \"An intestinal tuft cell that is a part of a vermiform appendix.\")\n23530:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-4183-8865\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009021 \"A stromal cell found in the lamina propria of the large intestine.\")\n23538:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-4183-8865\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009022 \"A stromal cell found in the lamina propria of the small intestine.\")\n23546:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-4183-8865\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009023 \"A T cell which resides in the Peyer's patch of the small intestine.\")\n23556:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-4183-8865\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009024 \"A mesothelial cell that is part of the small intestine.\")\n23564:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-4183-8865\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009025 \"A mesothelial cell that is part of the colon.\")\n23573:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009026 \"An enterocyte that is a part of a vermiform appendix.\")\n23585:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009027 \"A transit amplifying cell that is part of a crypt of Lieberkuhn of large intestine.\")\n23597:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20683682\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009028 \"An intestinal crypt stem cell that is located in the vermiform appendix. These stem cells reside at the bottom of crypts in the appendix and are highly proliferative. They either differentiate into transit amplifying cells or self-renew to form new stem cells.\")\n23610:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009029 \"A mesothelial cell that is located in a vermiform appendix.\")\n23621:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009030 \"An intestinal enteroendocrine cell that is located in a vermiform appendix.\")\n23633:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009031 \"A T cell that is located in a vermiform appendix.\")\n23645:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009032 \"A B cell that is located in a vermiform appendix.\")\n23657:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009033 \"A plasma cell that is located in a vermiform appendix.\")\n23669:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009034 \"A dendritic cell that is located in a vermiform appendix.\")\n23681:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009035 \"A stromal cell found in the lamina propria of the vermiform appendix.\")\n23691:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009036 \"A macrophage located in the vermiform appendix.\")\n23703:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:8011279\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-4183-8865/\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.arppress.org/v/vspfiles/assets/images/Chapter1T25LymphNodes.pdf\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009037 \"A B lymphocyte that resides in the mantle zone of the lymph node germinal center. These are generally IgM and IgD positive activated B cells that form a 'corona' around the germinal center and are part of the establishment of a secondary lymphatic follicule.\")\n23714:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009038 \"A macrophage that is located in the colon.\")\n23724:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009039 \"A goblet cell that is located in the colon.\")\n23733:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009040 \"A stromal cell found in the lamina propria of the colon.\")\n23742:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33079783\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35271673\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009041 \"A tuft cell that is part of the colonic epithelium, primarily adapted for microbial sensing in the dense colonic microbiota. Unlike its small intestinal counterpart, it does not participate in parasite-driven tuft cell–ILC2 circuits. Instead, it detects bacterial metabolites via taste-signaling pathways (Strine and Craig, 2022). The colonic tuft cell plays a key role in epithelial repair, modulates inflammatory responses through IL-25 secretion, and contributes to intestinal homeostasis by balancing microbiome interactions (Sebastian et al., 2021).\")\n23751:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009042 \"An enteroendocrine cell that is located in the colon.\")\n23761:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:10841502\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009043 \"An intestinal crypt stem cell that is located in the crypt of Lieberkuhn of colon.\")\n23769:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26551552\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4183-8865\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009044 \"A lymphocyte that resides in the lamina propria of the small intestine. Lamina propria leukocytes and intraepithelial lymphocytes are the effector compartments of the gut mucosal immune system. Lymphocytes circulate through gut associated lymphoid tissues until recruitment by intestinal antigens. They are involved in the gut immune response.\")\n23788:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-4183-8865\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009045 \"A B cell found in the lymph node medullary sinus.\")\n23797:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-4183-8865\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009046 \"A T cell found in the lymph node medullary sinus.\")\n23806:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-4183-8865\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009047 \"A macrophage found in the medullary sinus of the lymph node.\")\n23817:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009048 \"A macrophage that is located in the anorectum.\")\n23827:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27881983\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-4183-8865\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009049 \"A layer of smooth muscle cells that forms the outer layer of the high endothelial venule of lymph node and pumps to allow flow of lymph fluid carrying lymphocytes.\")\n23837:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009050 \"A B cell that is located in the anorectum.\")\n23846:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009051 \"A T cell that is located in the anorectum.\")\n23855:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009052 \"A smooth muscle cell that is located in the anorectum.\")\n23864:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009053 \"A stromal cell found in the lamina propria of the anorectum.\")\n23872:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009054 \"A microfold cell (M cell) that is part of the anorectum.\")\n23882:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009055 \"A paneth cell that is located in the anorectum.\")\n23892:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009056 \"A transit amplifying cell that is located in the anorectum.\")\n23901:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009057 \"A goblet cell that is located in the anorectum.\")\n23910:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009058 \"An enterocyte that is located in the anorectum.\")\n23919:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-4183-8865\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009059 \"A plasma cell that is located in the medullary sinus of the lymph node.\")\n23931:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WikipediaVersioned:Marginal_zone_B-cell&oldid=1032071222\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-4183-8865\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009060 \"A mature B cell located in the marginal zone of the lymph node.\")\n23941:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009061 \"An intestinal crypt stem cell that is located in the anorectum.\")\n23950:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21739669\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-4183-8865\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009062 \"A specialized type of CD4 positive T cell, the follicular helper T cell (TFH cell), that upregulates CXCR5 expression to enable its follicular localization. These specialised T cells reside in the germinal center of the lymph node.\")\n23961:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009063 \"An enteroendocrine cell that is located in the anorectum.\")\n23971:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-4183-8865\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009064 \"A T cell located in the lymph node paracortex, where macrophages and dendritic cells present antigenic peptides to these naïve T cells, stimulating them to become activated helper T cells or cytotoxic T lymphocytes.\")\n23982:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009065 \"An intestinal tuft cell that is located in the anorectum.\")\n23991:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009066 \"A stratified squamous epithelial cell that is part of the anal canal.\")\n24001:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17901585\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0002-7073-9172\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009067 \"An enterocyte found in the small intestine of newborn mammals and characterized by the presence of an apical canalicular system (ACS) leading to production of large vacuoles, important for colostral macromolecule uptake. After birth, the vacuolated fetal-type enterocytes are replaced with enterocytes lacking an ACS.\")\n24004:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33290721\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9610-7627\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0009067 \"early enterocyte\")\n24005:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33290721\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9610-7627\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0009067 \"immature enterocyte\")\n24128:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-4183-8865\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009080 \"A tuft cell located in the small intestine.\")\n24174:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4183-8865\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009084 \"An epithelial cell that is part of an endometrium glandular epithelium.\")\n24195:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4183-8865\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009086 \"An endothelial cell that is part of a respiratory system lymphatic vessel.\")\n24206:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4183-8865\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009087 \"An extravillous trophoblast that is polynuclear.\")\n24224:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4183-8865\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009089 \"A pericyte cell that is part of a lung.\")\n24236:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33419165\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WikipediaVersioned:Endothelial_colony_forming_cell&oldid=1068242094\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0002-0819-0473\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009090 \"An adult endothelial progenitor cell that is resident of adult vasculature and capable of differentiating to regenerate endothelial cell populations. Endothelial colony forming cells are characterised in vivo by clonal proliferative status, de novo vessel formation, homing to ischemic sites and paracrine support of angiogenesis. These cells are phenotypically similar to endothelial cells.\")\n24246:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21181888\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0002-0819-0473\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009091 \"A stem cell found in the interstitial compartment of the neonatal testis; it is capable of self-renewal as well as differentiation into steroidogenic cells (adult Leydig cells). Intermediate stages of development include progenitor Leydig cells and immature Leydig cells.\")\n24256:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4183-8865\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009092 \"An endothelial cell that is part of a placenta.\")\n24267:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4183-8865\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009093 \"A smooth muscle cell that is part of a placenta.\")\n24278:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30348985\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4183-8865\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009094 \"An endothelial cell that is part of a hepatic portal vein.\")\n24289:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4183-8865\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009095 \"An endothelial cell that is part of a uterus.\")\n24300:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11694559\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-2034-601X\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009096 \"Any cell that is part of the esophageal non-keratinized stratified squamous epithelium. In humans, the esophagus, which requires flexibility to accommodate swallowing of a bolus, is covered with a non-keratinized epithelium.\")\n24317:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32094117\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:7196501\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-2034-601X\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009097 \"A skeletal muscle fiber found in an embryo. In mammalian embryos, skeletal muscle expresses myosin heavy chain-embryonic (MyHC-emb, encoded by the MYH3 gene), which regulates skeletal muscle development.\")\n24325:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26180627\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:7196501\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-2034-601X\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009098 \"A skeletal muscle fiber found at the fetal and neonatal stages. In mammalian fetuses and neonates, skeletal muscle expresses myosin heavy chain-neonatal (MyHC-neo, encoded by the MYH8 gene). This expression disappears shortly after birth and is replaced by expression of adult heavy chain myosins.\")\n24343:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20209607\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:24814904\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7655-4833\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009100 \"A fibroblast located in the portal triad. Hepatic portal fibroblast are a non-parenchymal cell population located adjacent to bile duct epithelia in liver and are distinct from stellate cells. They differentiate into fibrogenic myofibroblasts during chronic injury states producing high levels of collagen.\")\n24363:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21435450\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22566825\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25998961\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28262465\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29752062\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34256989\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7655-4833\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009102 \"A specialized, fibroblastic reticular cell of mesenchymal origin found in lymph nodes. In human, it expresses several markers common to myofibroblasts (desmin, vimentin, CD73, CD90, α-smooth muscle actin (αSMA)), and can be differentiated from endothelial cells by its lack of CD31 expression. These cells are critical for the overall organization and function of the lymph node. Lymph node fibroblastic reticular cells (FRCs) can be further classified based on their location, function, and unique marker expression.\")\n24374:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21435450\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22566825\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25998961\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28262465\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29752062\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34256989\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7655-4833\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009103 \"A fibroblastic reticular cell found in the lymph node subcapsular sinus.\")\n24386:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21435450\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasD