tion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7655-4833\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009108 \"A lymphatic endothelial cell located in the subcapsular sinus floor of a lymph node. In human, it's characterized by a unique marker expression (TNFRSF9+).\")\n24450:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31402260\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32426372\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7655-4833\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009109 \"A lymphatic endothelial cell located in a lymph node trabecula.\")\n24462:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31402260\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32426372\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7655-4833\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009110 \"A lymphatic endothelial cell located in the ceiling part of a lymph node medulla.\")\n24473:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17067937\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7655-4833\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009111 \"A germinal center B cell found in a lymph node germinal center light zone.\")\n24484:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17067937\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7655-4833\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009112 \"A germinal center B cell found in a lymph node germinal center dark zone.\")\n24495:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15578096\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26501424\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29769249\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7655-4833\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009113 \"A regulatory T cell present in the B cell follicles and germinal centers of lymphoid tissues. In humans, it is CXCR5+.\")\n24506:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33324003\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7655-4833\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009114 \"A B cell found in the perisinusoidal area of a lymph node. In humans, monocytoid B cells are a morphologically distinct B cell population\n24517:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7655-4833\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009115 \"An endothelial cell located in a lymph node lymphatic vessel.\")\n24525:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19063729\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20346151\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21930782\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4412-7970\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009116 \"A progenitor cell with the potential to differentiate into luminal epithelial cells of mammary glands. In mouse, CD61 and c-kit were found to be coexpressed by the majority of, but not all, committed luminal progenitor cells.\")\n24535:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/417>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:2478566\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28445731\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30420661\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0010000 \"A differentiating matrix keratinocyte that has initiated terminal differentiation and keratin synthesis. This cell undergoes a characteristic change while migrating upward from the hair follicle bulb, representing a committed progenitor cell destined to form the hair medulla, cortex and hair root sheath.\")\n24611:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1016/j.cnp.2022.11.002\") foaf:depiction obo:CL_0010010 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/CB_circuits_PMID3650468_f2.png>)\n24612:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.3389/fnins.2020.00293\") foaf:depiction obo:CL_0010010 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/Candelabrum_cell.jpg>)\n24743:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1016/j.cnp.2022.11.002\") foaf:depiction obo:CL_0011006 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/CB_circuits_PMID3650468_f2.png>)\n24744:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.3389/fnins.2020.00293\") foaf:depiction obo:CL_0011006 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/Candelabrum_cell.jpg>)\n24787:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9900-7880\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0011012 \"A cell of the neural crest. Neural crest cells are multipotent. Premigratory neural crest cells are found at the neural plate boarder, some of which will undergo ectomesynchymal transition and delamination to form migratory neural crest cells.\")\n24815:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30612620\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.lexico.com/en/definition/flagellum\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0011016 \"A motile sperm cell that contains a slender threadlike microscopic appendage that enables motion.\")\n24901:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:978-1-62808-994-3\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.1016/B978-0-12-409503-8.00002-0\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0011026 \"A precursor cell that has a tendency to differentiate into a specific type of cell. They are descendants of stem cells, only they are more constrained in their differentiation potential or capacity for self-renewal, and are often more limited in both senses.\")\n24909:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28369879\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6164-0667\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0011027 \"Any fibroblast that is part of skeletal muscle tissue.\")\n24927:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cnidocyte\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2825-0621\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0011029 \"An explosive cell containing one giant secretory organelle called a cnidocyst (also known as a cnida (plural cnidae) or nematocyst) that contains a toxin responsible for the stings delivered by a cnidarian to other organisms. Cnidae are used to capture prey and as a defense against predators. The presence of cnidocytes defines the phylum Cnidaria (corals, sea anemones, hydrae, jellyfish, etc.).\")\n24956:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31474562\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1009-339X\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2244-7917\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0011032 \"An enterocyte that possesses a large supranuclear vacuolar system that preferentially internalizes dietary protein via receptor-mediated and fluid-phase endocytosis for intracellular digestion and trans-cellular transport. In zebrafish these cells are located in the posterior region of the mid intestine throughout life. In mammals they are found in the ileum pre-weaning and later are replaced by mature enterocytes.\")\n24960:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33290721\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9610-7627\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0011032 \"early enterocyte\")\n24961:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33290721\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9610-7627\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0011032 \"immature enterocyte\")\n25140:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33842835\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0001-7772-9578\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0017002 \"A neuroendocrine cell that is part of the prostate epithelium.\")\n25156:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D000067170\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20367664\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28714595\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31311805\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Telocyte\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0017004 \"A supportive cell with a small, oval-shaped body and one to five telopodes. Telopodes are cytoplasmic protrusions from tens to hundreds of micrometers long and mostly below 0.2 microns of caliber.\")\n25162:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <https://doi.org/10.1016/B978-0-12-818561-2.00001-1>) rdfs:comment obo:CL_0017004 \"Telocytes manage to develop complex networks in almost all organs of the human body. Although staining positively for vimentin antibody, some uncertainty still persists over the mesenchymal origin of these cells.\")\n25169:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"NCIT:C13013\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0001-9990-8331\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0017005 \"A lymphocyte that has gotten larger after being stimulated by an antigen.\")\n25181:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"EFO:0005293\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2825-0621\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0017006 \"A lymphocyte of B lineage that has gotten larger after being stimulated by an antigen.\")\n25204:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <http://orcid.org/0000-0001-7772-9578>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30566875\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0017010 \"A hillock cell that is part of the urethra.\")\n25213:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <http://orcid.org/0000-0001-7772-9578>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30566875\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0017011 \"A hillock cell that is part of the prostatic urethra.\")\n25492:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:license \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35927027\") foaf:depiction obo:CL_0020003 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/GPi_core_shell_myamoto.jpg>)\n25613:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q934475\") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_0020014 \"photosensitive ganglion cell\")\n28199:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <https://doi.org/10.1152/physrev.1998.78.3.723>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Intraglomerular_mesangial_cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_1000742 \"A mesangial cell located among the glomerular capillaries in a renal corpuscle.\")\n28202:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9127003\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.1152/physrev.1998.78.3.723\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_1000742 \"Like smooth muscle, a glomerular mesangial cell is contractile and possesses the filaments actin and myosin. The contractile mechanism is also similar to that of smooth muscle, with Ca2+/calmodulin-activated myosin light-chain kinase instigating myosin-actin cross-bridge cycling. Mesangial cell phagocytosis of apoptotic neutrophils involves a novel CD36-independent, alpha(v)beta3/TSP-mediated mechanism that is uncoupled from chemokine secretion, emphasizing the injury-limiting potential of mesangial cell phagocytosis of apoptotic cells.\")\n28760:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_1001432 \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Collecting_duct_system#Intercalated_cells\")\n28930:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"NPX:PDR\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_1001572 \"A vascular endothelial cell found in colon blood vessels.\")\n29267:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7073-9172>) obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_1100001 \"An epithelial cell that is specialised for the synthesis and secretion of specific biomolecules.\")\n29526:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1016/j.cnp.2022.11.002\") foaf:depiction obo:CL_2000027 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/CB_circuits_PMID3650468_f2.png>)\n29527:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.3389/fnins.2020.00293\") foaf:depiction obo:CL_2000027 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/Candelabrum_cell.png>)\n30255:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:CellBLAST\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30096314\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31554486\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35858549\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Sensory_neuron\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.britannica.com/science/sensory-neuron\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK539846/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_3000004 \"A neuron type that is located in a peripheral nervous system and it transmits sensory information from the peripheral (PNS) to the central nervous system (CNS). A sensory neuron converts physical (light, sound, touch) or chemical (such as taste and smell) stimuli into an electrical signal through a process known as sensory transduction. The function of a sensory neuron is to carry informations from the external environment and internal body conditions to the central nervous system for further processing.\")\n30392:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30382198\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/e4ddac12-f48f-4455-8e8d-c2a48a683437.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023011 \"A transcriptomically distinct GABAergic neuron located in the cerebral cortex that expresses Lamp5.\")\n30439:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33186530\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/e4ddac12-f48f-4455-8e8d-c2a48a683437.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023015 \"A transcriptomically distinct GABAergic neuron located in the cerebral cortex that expresses Gamma-synuclein.\")\n30451:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33186530\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/e4ddac12-f48f-4455-8e8d-c2a48a683437.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023016 \"A transcriptomically distinct GABAergic neuron derived from the CGE and that expresses the vasoactive intestinal polypeptide. Its soma is located in the forebrain.\")\n30473:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27477017\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33742131\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/9c63201d-bfd9-41a8-bbbc-18d947556f3d.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023017 \"A transcriptomically distinct GABAergic neuron located in the cerebral cortex that expresses somatostatin (sst) and derived from the MGE.\")\n30488:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27477017\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/9c63201d-bfd9-41a8-bbbc-18d947556f3d.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023018 \"A transcriptomically distinct GABAergic interneuron with a soma located in the pallium. These neurons express Parvalbumin.\")\n30585:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7258-9596\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4023026 \"dopamine 1 medium spiny neuron\")\n30628:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7258-9596\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4023029 \"dopamine 2 medium spiny neuron\")\n30724:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.1101/2020.10.19.34312\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30382198\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/d01c9dff-abd1-4825-bf30-2eb2ba74597e.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023038 \"A glutamatergic neuron with a soma found in cortical layer 6b. They are transcriptomically related to corticothalamic-projecting neurons but have differential projections to the thalamus or anterior cingulate.\")\n30741:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34616075\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/c3aa4f95-7a18-4a7d-8dd8-ca324d714363.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023040 \"An intratelencephalic-projecting glutamatergic neuron with a soma found in cortical layers L2/3-6.\")\n30751:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34616075\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/d01c9dff-abd1-4825-bf30-2eb2ba74597e.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023041 \"A transcriptomically distinct glutamatergic neuron, with a soma found in the deeper portion of L5, that has long-range axonal projections including deep subcortical targets outside of the telencephalon and, in some cases, the spinal cord. While the L5 ET neuron projections are not limited to ET targets, they are clearly differentiated from the neuron subclasses whose projections are constrained to intratelencephalic (IT) targets. L5 ET neurons are generally the largest excitatory cortical neurons, typically having a thick apical dendrite with a prominent dendritic tuft in layer 1 and displaying burst-firing physiological characteristics.\")\n30767:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34616075\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/d01c9dff-abd1-4825-bf30-2eb2ba74597e.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023042 \"A transcriptomically distinct corticothalamic-projecting neuron with a soma found in cortical layer 6.\")\n30778:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31209381\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34616075\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/d01c9dff-abd1-4825-bf30-2eb2ba74597e.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023043 \"A transcriptomically distinct near-projecting glutamatergic neuron with a soma found in layer 5/6 of the primary motor cortex. The standard transcriptomic reference data for this cell type can be found on the CellxGene census under the collection: 'Transcriptomic cytoarchitecture reveals principles of human neocortex organization', dataset: 'Supercluster: Deep layer (non-IT) excitatory neurons', Author Categories: 'CrossArea_subclass', cluster L5/6 NP.\")\n30875:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27284195\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29443965\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30096314\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/5346f9c6-755e-4336-94cc-38706ec00c2f.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023051 \"A transcriptomically distinct type of mesothelial fibroblast that is derived from the neural crest, is localized on blood vessels, and is a key component of the pia and arachnoid membranes surrounding the brain. The standard transcriptomic reference data for this cell type can be found on the CellxGene census under the collection: 'Transcriptomic cytoarchitecture reveals principles of human neocortex organization', dataset: 'Supercluster: Non-neuronal cells', Author Categories: 'CrossArea_subclass', clusters VLMC.\")\n31501:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15845086\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31209381\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33372656\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/9c63201d-bfd9-41a8-bbbc-18d947556f3d.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023121 \"A transcriptomically distinct sst GABAergic interneuron that also expresses Chodl. These neurons are rare and correspond to the only known interneurons with long-range projection.\")\n31635:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1016/j.cnp.2022.11.002\") foaf:depiction obo:CL_4023161 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/CB_circuits_PMID3650468_f2.png>)\n31636:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.3389/fnins.2020.00293\") foaf:depiction obo:CL_4023161 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/Candelabrum_cell.jpg>)\n31685:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK539823/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023170 \"A trigeminal neuron that is responsible for sensation in the face.\")\n31693:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK539823/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023171 \"A trigeminal neuron that is responsible for motor functions such as biting and chewing.\")\n31700:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7258-9596>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26778959\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9579598\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023181 \"A neurecto-epithelial cell that is part of the basal layer of the subcommissural organ and specializes in the secretion of proteins into the subarachnoid space. Hypendymal cells have similar characteristics to ependymal cells and express SCO-spondin.\")\n31849:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31819095\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0002-0819-0473\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030000 \"A melanocyte located in the vascular uvea and involved in photoprotection, regulation of oxidative damage and immune responses.\")\n31866:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2825-0621\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030002 \"An alpha-beta memory T cell with the phenotype CD45RA-positive.\")\n31872:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/T_cell#Memory_T_cells\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4030002 \"terminally differentiated effector memory cells re-expressing CD45RA\")\n31886:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thymic_nurse_cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030004 \"A large epithelial cell found in the thymus. This cell type may internalize thymocytes through extensions of plasma membrane. The cell surface and cytoplasmic vacuoles of a thymic nurse cell express MHC Class I and MHC Class II antigens. The interaction of these antigens with a developing thymocyte determines whether the thymocyte undergoes positive or negative selection.\")\n31903:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.1186/1477-7827-7-129\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.3390/cells8080933\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.proteinatlas.org/learn/dictionary/normal/fallopian+tube\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030006 \"An epithelial cell that is part of the fallopian tube that secretes mucus and oviduct-specific products in response to hormonal stimulation from estrogen and luteinizing hormone. This fallopian tube secretory cell is similar in height to the ciliated cell, but typically exhibits a more narrow, columnar shape. Its nucleus is ovoid and oriented perpendicular to the cell's long axis, with denser chromatin and a smaller nucleolus compared to the ciliated cell.\")\n31908:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ccr.2013.10.013\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.proteinatlas.org/learn/dictionary/normal/fallopian+tube\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4030006 \"The other cell types of the fallopian tube epithelium include the ciliated cell and the intercalary cell, or peg cell. The fallopian tube secretory epithelial cell type has been implicated as a source of high-grade serous ovarian carcinoma.\")\n31916:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16565155\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.proteinatlas.org/humanproteome/tissue/fallopian+tube\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030007 \"A multi-ciliated epithelial cell that is part of the fallopian tube, mainly found on the apex of the mucosal folds. This cell exhibits a columnar shape with an oval nucleus and is characterized by the presence of cilia on its surface. The coordinated beating of these cilia, together with peristaltic contractions, contributes to the self-propulsion of spermatozoa, the transport of ovum during ovulation and the transport of the fertilized ovum to the intramural fallopian tube.\")\n31979:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <http://orcid.org/0000-0003-2804-127X>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33769951\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030013 \"Epithelial cell of the descending thin limb of the long loop (juxtamedullary) nephron that spans the outer medulla (inner stripe). It is known in some mammalian species that the long descending limb of the loop of Henle in the outer medulla selectively expresses the secreted activin-antagonist protein follistatin (Fst), the GPI-linked adhesion protein Cdh13, and the protein kinase Stk32a.\")\n31988:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <http://orcid.org/0000-0003-2804-127X>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33769951\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/gene/8170\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030014 \"Epithelial cell of the descending thin limb of the long loop (juxtamedullary) nephron that spans the inner medulla. It is known in some mammalian species that the long descending limb of the loop of Henle in the inner medulla selectively expresses the nuclear receptor Nr2e3, the Ig kappa chain Igkc, and the secreted protein dermokine (Dmkn). SLC14A2, which expresses a urea transporter, is also expressed in the inner medulla.\")\n32006:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <http://orcid.org/0000-0003-2804-127X>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:24855283\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030016 \"An epithelial cell located in the early distal convoluted tubule.\")\n32014:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <http://orcid.org/0000-0003-2804-127X>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:24855283\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030017 \"An epithelial cell located in the late distal convoluted tubule.\")\n32023:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <http://orcid.org/0000-0003-2804-127X>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27582101\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31249312\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030018 \"A renal principal cell located in the connecting tubule.\")\n32057:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <https://doi.org/10.1101/2021.07.28.454201>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:10559635\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030022 \"A fibroblast that is located in the renal medulla interstitium.\")\n32066:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7772-9578>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30069044\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32726565\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33442032\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030023 \"A hillock cell that is located in respiratory epithelium. In some mammalian species, this cell type has been noted to express KRT13 and KRT4 and is postulated to play a role in squamous barrier function and immunomodulation.\")\n32091:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7431-4139>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:24223998\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35176508\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030026 \"An enterocyte of the human intestine expressing bestrophin-4 (BEST4) calcium-activated ion channels.\")\n32099:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2020.08.013\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030027 \"An amacrine cell that uses GABA as a neurotransmitter.\")\n32107:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2020.08.013\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030028 \"An amacrine cell that uses glycine as a neurotransmitter.\")\n32115:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9990-8331>) obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030029 \"A lymphocyte located in blood.\")\n32122:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9990-8331>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2534-198X>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31092833\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://sciencing.com/what-peripheral-blood-4672930.html\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030030 \"A blood lymphocyte located in the flowing, circulating blood of the body.\")\n32139:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7655-4833>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25311230\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2017.0580\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.1161/ATVBAHA.120.314789\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.1161/JAHA.117.006339\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.2353/ajpath.2007.070251\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030032 \"An interstitial cell that is part of a cardiac valve leaflet. Along with valve endothelial cells, a valve interstitial cell maintains tissue homeostasis for the function of cardiac valves through secreting biochemical signals, matrix proteins and matrix remodeling enzymes.\")\n32172:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2825-0621>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.1177/154405910208100806\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030035 \"A dental pulp cell that possesses stem-cell-like qualities, including self-renewal capability and multi-lineage differentiation.\")\n32181:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.proteinatlas.org/humanproteome/single+cell+type/Germ+cells#earlyspermatids\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030036 \"A spermatid in an early stage of maturation that has a round morphology and is transcriptionally active.\")\n32183:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.1016/B978-0-323-01970-5.50014-2\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4030036 \"round spermatid\")\n32191:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.proteinatlas.org/humanproteome/single+cell+type/Germ+cells#latespermatids\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030037 \"A spermatid in a late stage of maturation that has an elongated morphology and is transcriptionally inert when the acrosome is fully developed.\")\n32193:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.1016/B978-0-323-01970-5.50014-2\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4030037 \"elongated spermatid\")\n32204:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.1002/stem.1130\") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_4030038 \"CD133+CD24+CD106- tubular cell\")\n32227:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31290979\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37999981\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1016/j.coemr.2024.100503\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1038/s41591-020-1040-z\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.proteinatlas.org/humanproteome/single+cell+type/Glandular+epithelial+cells#endometrialciliatedcells\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030040 \"A multi-ciliated cell of the endometrial epithelium. This cell is characterized by the presence of 9+2 motile cilia on its apical surface, which facilitates the movement of mucus across the endometrial surface.\")\n32412:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9990-8331>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26074923\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030058 \"A macrophage that expresses the T cell receptor complex at the cell surface.\")\n32424:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25622573\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34004146\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37292694\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/c3aa4f95-7a18-4a7d-8dd8-ca324d714363.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030059 \"A transcriptomically distinct intratelencephalic-projecting glutamatergic neuron with a soma found between cortical layer 2-4. This intratelencephalic-projecting glutamatergic neuron has thin-tufted apical dendrites and extends its axonal projection into L5 in the neocortex. This neuronal type has a hyperpolarised resting membrane potential.\")\n32466:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37292694\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/c3aa4f95-7a18-4a7d-8dd8-ca324d714363.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030063 \"A transcriptomically distinct intratelencephalic-projecting glutamatergic neuron with a soma found in cortical layer 3-4. This neuron type can have a pyramidal, star-pyramidal or spiny stellate morphology and projects its output to L2/3 and L5A/B.\")\n32477:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37292694\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37609206\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/c3aa4f95-7a18-4a7d-8dd8-ca324d714363.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030064 \"An intratelencephalic-projecting glutamatergic neuron with a soma found in cortical layer 5.\")\n32488:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37292694\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37609206\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/c3aa4f95-7a18-4a7d-8dd8-ca324d714363.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030065 \"A transcriptomically distinct intratelencephalic-projecting glutamatergic neuron with a soma found in L6 of the primary motor cortex. These cells are short untufted pyramidal cells, which could be stellate or inverted.\")\n32535:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7258-9596\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4032000 \"club-like cell of the prostatic urethra epithelium\")\n32648:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22375063\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35883599\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9520465\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.proteinatlas.org/humanproteome/single+cell+type/squamous+epithelial+cells#suprabasalkeratinocytes\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033013 \"A keratinocyte that resides in the epidermal suprabasal layer and expresses differentiation markers, including keratin 1 and keratin 10, in both humans and mice. In human interfollicular epidermis, this cell retains proliferative capacity and possesses retrodifferentiation potential, acquiring basal-like properties during wound healing or basement membrane contact.\")\n33037:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.1111/j.1096-3642.1981.tb01137.x\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:10052456\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28655883\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.nejohnston.org/Birds/documents/AvianTongues_Johnston.pdf\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033049 \"A taste receptor cell that is part of a taste bud of a tongue.\")\n33049:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:10191060\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12128258\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34880760\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2244-7917\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4033050 \"Frequently used when describing the developing nervous system in zebrafish. A catecholaminergic neuron expresses tyrosine hydroxylase (TH), tyrosine hydroxylase 2 (TH2), aromatic amino acid decarboxylase (AADC), dopamine b-hydroxylase (DBH), and phenylethanolamine-N-methyl transferase (PEMT), which are enzymes necessary for catecholamine synthesis.\")\n33119:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19648928\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35617956\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://nrs.harvard.edu/URN-3:HUL.INSTREPOS:37368328\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033057 \"A luminal epithelial cell of the mammary gland that can proliferate and has the potential to differentiate into a lactocyte during pregnancy. In humans, a luminal adaptive secretory precursor cell can be identified by high levels of the markers EpCAM and CD49f, and in mice it can be identified by low levels of CD29 and high levels of CD14, Kit, CD61, and Tspan8.\")\n33128:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://nrs.harvard.edu/URN-3:HUL.INSTREPOS:37368328\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033057 \"ER-negative luminal alveolar progenitor\")\n33129:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://nrs.harvard.edu/URN-3:HUL.INSTREPOS:37368328\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033057 \"AP\")\n33131:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033057 \"LASP\")\n33140:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19648928\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26390871\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34156490\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://nrs.harvard.edu/URN-3:HUL.INSTREPOS:37368328\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033058 \"A luminal epithelial cell of the mammary gland that transduces endocrine cues to orchestrate proliferation, architectural remodeling, and differentiation of other cells in the mammary gland via paracrine signaling. This cell expresses high levels of estrogen receptors. In humans, a luminal hormone-sensing cell can be identified by high levels of EpCAM and low levels of CD49f, and in mice it can be identified by low levels of CD29 and high levels of Foxa1, CD133, and Sca1 (Ly6a).\")\n33148:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://nrs.harvard.edu/URN-3:HUL.INSTREPOS:37368328\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033058 \"ER-positive luminal hormone-sensor cell\")\n33151:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033058 \"LHS\")\n33153:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26390871\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34156490\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4969-670X\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4033058 \"Following lineage specification, a luminal hormone-sensing cell expresses receptors for one or more hormones, such as estrogens, progesterone, androgens, and prolactin. In response to progesterone, luminal hormone-sensing cells express TNFSF11, WNT4, and RSPO1, among other factors, which cause branching, proliferation, and partial differentiation in LASP and B-Myo cells during luteal phases of the estrous/menstrual cycle and during gestation. During ductal elongation, ER activity drives expression of AREG in LHS cells, which is necessary for proliferation of the epithelium to fill the mammary fat pad.\")\n33277:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4033083 \"Often in literature squamous granulosa cell and pre-granulosa cell are used as synonyms. However, this term only makes reference to the quiescent granulosa cells that surround the primordial ovarian follicle, while a pre-granulosa cell proliferates to form the primordial follicle (and thus cells become the squamous granulosa cells).\")\n33438:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:license <http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26402712\") Annotation(rdfs:comment \"Schematic of the conventional outflow pathway, showing the Schlemm's canal (SC, green) and the trabecular meshwork (TM, orange). The left inset shows an expanded view of the Schlemm’s canal’s microanatomy detailing the cell morphology of the inner and outer wall endocrine cells.\") foaf:depiction obo:CL_4033097 \"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/Schlemms_canal_endo_cell_PMID26402712.png\"^^xsd:anyURI)\n33449:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:license <http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26402712\") Annotation(rdfs:comment \"Schematic of the conventional outflow pathway, showing the Schlemm's canal (SC, green) and the trabecular meshwork (TM, orange). The left inset shows an expanded view of the Schlemm’s canal’s microanatomy detailing the cell morphology of the inner and outer wall endocrine cells. The inner wall endocrine cells, shown in blue, line the canal surface facing the trabecular meshwork. Some of the inner wall cells contain giant vacuoles.\") foaf:depiction obo:CL_4033098 \"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/Schlemms_canal_endo_cell_PMID26402712.png\"^^xsd:anyURI)\n33459:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:license <http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26402712\") Annotation(rdfs:comment \"Schematic of the conventional outflow pathway, showing the Schlemm's canal (SC, green) and the trabecular meshwork (TM, orange). The left inset shows an expanded view of the Schlemm’s canal’s microanatomy detailing the cell morphology of the inner and outer wall endocrine cells. The outer wall endocrine cells, shown in green, line the side of Schlemm’s canal facing the collector channels and venous system.\") foaf:depiction obo:CL_4033099 \"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/Schlemms_canal_endo_cell_PMID26402712.png\"^^xsd:anyURI)\n33505:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0819-0473\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4040003 \"fetal pre-type 2 pneumocyte\")\n33514:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0819-0473>) obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4040004 \"Any mesenchymal stem cell of adipose tissue that is part of an orbital region.\")\n33674:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34004146\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36007006\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824669\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/e4ddac12-f48f-4455-8e8d-c2a48a683437.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4042013 \"A transcriptomically distinct GABAergic interneuron marked by Lamp5 and Lhx6 expression, derived from the Medial Ganglionic Eminence (MGE), and located in the pallium.\")\n33717:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_4042016 \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/9f222629-9e39-47d0-b83f-e08d610c7479.cxg/\")\n33733:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(terms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <doi:10.3389/fendo.2019.00401>) foaf:depiction obo:CL_4042017 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/fendo-10-00401-g001.jpg>)\n33734:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <doi:10.3389/fnins.2022.1129414>) Annotation(rdfs:comment \"α1 tanycytes are the most dorsally located subtype, followed by α2 tanycytes, then β1 tanycytes, and finally β2 tanycytes which occupy the ventricular floor. 3V, third ventricle; Arc, arcuate nucleus; DMH, dorsomedial hypothalamic nucleus; VMH, ventromedial hypothalamic nucleus.\") foaf:depiction obo:CL_4042017 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/fnins-16-1129414-g001.jpg>)\n33747:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(terms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <doi:10.3389/fendo.2019.00401>) foaf:depiction obo:CL_4042018 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/fendo-10-00401-g001.jpg>)\n33748:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <doi:10.3389/fnins.2022.1129414>) Annotation(rdfs:comment \"α1 tanycytes are the most dorsally located subtype, followed by α2 tanycytes, then β1 tanycytes, and finally β2 tanycytes which occupy the ventricular floor. 3V, third ventricle; Arc, arcuate nucleus; DMH, dorsomedial hypothalamic nucleus; VMH, ventromedial hypothalamic nucleus.\") foaf:depiction obo:CL_4042018 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/fnins-16-1129414-g001.jpg>)\n33760:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(terms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <doi:10.3389/fendo.2019.00401>) foaf:depiction obo:CL_4042019 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/fendo-10-00401-g001.jpg>)\n33761:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <doi:10.3389/fnins.2022.1129414>) Annotation(rdfs:comment \"α1 tanycytes are the most dorsally located subtype, followed by α2 tanycytes, then β1 tanycytes, and finally β2 tanycytes which occupy the ventricular floor. 3V, third ventricle; Arc, arcuate nucleus; DMH, dorsomedial hypothalamic nucleus; VMH, ventromedial hypothalamic nucleus.\") foaf:depiction obo:CL_4042019 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/fnins-16-1129414-g001.jpg>)\n33776:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(terms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <doi:10.3389/fendo.2019.00401>) foaf:depiction obo:CL_4042020 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/fendo-10-00401-g001.jpg>)\n33777:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <doi:10.3389/fnins.2022.1129414>) Annotation(rdfs:comment \"α1 tanycytes are the most dorsally located subtype, followed by α2 tanycytes, then β1 tanycytes, and finally β2 tanycytes which occupy the ventricular floor. 3V, third ventricle; Arc, arcuate nucleus; DMH, dorsomedial hypothalamic nucleus; VMH, ventromedial hypothalamic nucleus.\") foaf:depiction obo:CL_4042020 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/fnins-16-1129414-g001.jpg>)\n33895:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.3389/fnins.2020.00293\") foaf:depiction obo:CL_4042030 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/Candelabrum_cell.jpg>)\n33919:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/e4ddac12-f48f-4455-8e8d-c2a48a683437.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4042032 \"A transcriptomically distinct GABAergic neuron, located in the cerebral cortex and derived from the CGE, that expresses the transcript PAX6.\")\n33997:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12593982\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12637172\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20130169\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK98190/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4042039 \"A neuron of the central nervous system that develops from a caudal ganglionic eminence.\")\n34000:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12593982\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12637172\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20130169\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK98190/\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4042039 \"Neurons derived from the caudal ganglionic eminence consist mostly of neurons populating the cortical layers of the brain and some subcortical areas such as the globus pallidus, the striatus and the hippocampus. Amongst neurons derived from the caudal ganglionic eminence there are cortical GABAergic neurons such as Pax6, Lamp5, VIP, sncg, GABAergic; in the hippocampus, mossy fibers, pyramidal neurons, granule neurons and interneurons; in the striatum and globus pallidus, medium spiny projection neurons.\")\n34512:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18480313\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32375819\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK27998/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4052017 \"A capillary endothelial cell that is part of the choroid plexus, characterized by its fenestrated nature with 60 to 80 nm fenestrations and lack of tight junctions. This fenestrated structure allows for the rapid delivery of water and other components, aiding in the production of cerebrospinal fluid (CSF).\")\n34897:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0009-0000-8480-9277\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4052055 \"mature NK T lymphocyte, human\")\n34898:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0009-0000-8480-9277\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4052055 \"mature NK T-cell, human\")\n34899:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0009-0000-8480-9277\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4052055 \"mature NK T-lymphocyte, human\")\n34900:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0009-0000-8480-9277\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4052055 \"mature NKT cell, human\")\n34901:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0009-0000-8480-9277\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4052055 \"mature natural killer T cell, human\")\n34902:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0009-0000-8480-9277\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4052055 \"mature natural killer T lymphocyte, human\")\n34903:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0009-0000-8480-9277\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4052055 \"mature natural killer T-lymphocyte, human\")\n35330:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_4072022 \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/e4ddac12-f48f-4455-8e8d-c2a48a683437.cxg/\")\n35332:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://zenodo.org/records/11165918\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4072022 \"The marker set CHST9, LAMP5 can identify the Human cell type Lamp5 Lhx6 neuron in the neocortex with a confidence of 0.821678322 (NS-Forest FBeta value).\")\n35345:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27477017\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33742131\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/9c63201d-bfd9-41a8-bbbc-18d947556f3d.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072027 \"A transcriptomically distinct GABAergic neuron located in the cerebral cortex that expresses somatostatin (sst). The standard transcriptomic reference data for this cell type can be found on the CellxGene census under the collection: 'Transcriptomic cytoarchitecture reveals principles of human neocortex organization', dataset: 'Supercluster: MGE-derived interneurons', Author Categories: 'CrossArea_subclass', cluster Sst.\")\n35363:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27477017\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/9c63201d-bfd9-41a8-bbbc-18d947556f3d.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072029 \"A transcriptomically distinct GABAergic interneuron with a soma located in a cerebral cortex and it expresses Parvalbumin. The standard transcriptomic reference data for this cell type can be found on the CellxGene census under the collection: 'Transcriptomic cytoarchitecture reveals principles of human neocortex organization', dataset: 'Supercluster: MGE-derived interneurons', Author Categories: 'CrossArea_subclass', cluster Pvalb.\")\n35376:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15845086\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31209381\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33372656\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/9c63201d-bfd9-41a8-bbbc-18d947556f3d.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072031 \"A transcriptomically distinct sst GABAergic interneuron that also expresses Chodl. These neurons are rare and correspond to the only known interneurons with long-range projection. The standard transcriptomic reference data for this cell type can be found on the CellxGene census under the collection: 'Transcriptomic cytoarchitecture reveals principles of human neocortex organization', dataset: 'Supercluster: MGE-derived interneurons', Author Categories: 'CrossArea_subclass', clusters Sst Chodl.\")\n35382:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.11165918\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4072031 \"The marker set NPY can identify the Human cell type sst chodl GABAergic interneuron in the neocortex with a confidence of 0.894026187 (NS-Forest FBeta value).\")\n35391:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33186530\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/e4ddac12-f48f-4455-8e8d-c2a48a683437.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072032 \"A transcriptomically distinct GABAergic neuron that expresses the vasoactive intestinal polypeptide and that has its soma located in the forebrain. The standard transcriptomic reference data for this cell type can be found on the CellxGene census under the collection: 'Transcriptomic cytoarchitecture reveals principles of human neocortex organization', dataset: 'Supercluster: CGE-derived interneurons', Author Categories: 'CrossArea_subclass', cluster Vip.\")\n35402:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.11165918\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4072032 \"The marker set VIP can identify the Human cell type VIP GABAergic interneuron in the neocortex with a confidence of 0.855531344 (NS-Forest FBeta value).\")\n35412:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30382198\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/e4ddac12-f48f-4455-8e8d-c2a48a683437.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072034 \"A transcriptomically distinct GABAergic neuron located in the cerebral cortex that expresses Lamp5. The standard transcriptomic reference data for this cell type can be found on the CellxGene census under the collection: 'Transcriptomic cytoarchitecture reveals principles of human neocortex organization', dataset: 'Supercluster: CGE-derived interneurons', Author Categories: 'CrossArea_subclass', clusters Lamp5.\")\n35418:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.11165918\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4072034 \"The marker set LINC00298, KIT can identify the Human cell type lamp5 GABAergic interneuron in the neocortex with a confidence of 0.814687838 (NS-Forest FBeta value).\")\n35427:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33186530\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/e4ddac12-f48f-4455-8e8d-c2a48a683437.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072035 \"A transcriptomically distinct GABAergic neuron located in the cerebral cortex that expresses Gamma-synuclein. The standard transcriptomic reference data for this cell type can be found on the CellxGene census under the collection: 'Transcriptomic cytoarchitecture reveals principles of human neocortex organization', dataset: 'Supercluster: CGE-derived interneurons', Author Categories: 'CrossArea_subclass', clusters Sncg.\")\n35434:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.11165918\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4072035 \"The marker set RXRG, THSD7B can identify the Human cell type sncg GABAergic interneuron in the neocortex with a confidence of 0.628943702 (NS-Forest FBeta value).\")\n35444:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/e4ddac12-f48f-4455-8e8d-c2a48a683437.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072036 \"A transcriptomically distinct GABAergic neuron located in the cerebral cortex that expresses the transcript PAX6. The standard transcriptomic reference data for this cell type can be found on the CellxGene census under the collection: 'Transcriptomic cytoarchitecture reveals principles of human neocortex organization', dataset: 'Supercluster: CGE-derived interneurons', Author Categories: 'CrossArea_subclass', clusters PAX\")\n35448:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.11165918\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4072036 \"The marker set RELN, HCRTR2 can identify the Human cell type PAX6 GABAergic interneuron in the neocortex with a confidence of 0.724125093 (NS-Forest FBeta value).\")\n35457:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25622573\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34004146\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37292694\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/c3aa4f95-7a18-4a7d-8dd8-ca324d714363.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072037 \"A transcriptomically distinct intratelencephalic-projecting glutamatergic neuron with a soma found between cortical layer 2-4. This intratelencephalic-projecting glutamatergic neuron has thin-tufted apical dendrites and extends its axonal projection into L5 in the neocortex. This neuronal type has a hyperpolarised resting membrane potential. The standard transcriptomic reference data for this cell type can be found on the CellxGene census under the collection: 'Transcriptomic cytoarchitecture reveals principles of human neocortex organization', dataset: 'Supercluster: IT-projecting excitatory neurons', Author Categories: 'CrossArea_subclass', clusters L2/3 IT.\")\n35464:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.11165918\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4072037 \"The marker set ONECUT2, COL5A2 can identify the Human cell type L2/3 intratelencephalic projecting glutamatergic neuron in the neocortex with a confidence of 0.670149932 (NS-Forest FBeta value).\")\n35473:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37292694\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37609206\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/c3aa4f95-7a18-4a7d-8dd8-ca324d714363.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072038 \"An intratelencephalic-projecting glutamatergic neuron with a soma found in cortical layer 5. The standard transcriptomic reference data for this cell type can be found on the CellxGene census under the collection: 'Transcriptomic cytoarchitecture reveals principles of human neocortex organization', dataset: 'Supercluster: IT-projecting excitatory neurons', Author Categories: 'CrossArea_subclass', L5 IT.\")\n35480:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.11165918\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4072038 \"The marker set ARSJ, RORB, KCNK2 can identify the Human cell type L5 intratelencephalic projecting glutamatergic neuron in the neocortex with a confidence of 0.764261336 (NS-Forest FBeta value).\")\n35489:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37292694\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/c3aa4f95-7a18-4a7d-8dd8-ca324d714363.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072039 \"A transcriptomically distinct intratelencephalic-projecting glutamatergic neuron with a soma found in cortical layer 3-4. This neuron type can have a pyramidal, star-pyramidal or spiny stellate morphology and projects its output to L2/3 and L5A/B. The standard transcriptomic reference data for this cell type can be found on the CellxGene census under the collection: 'Transcriptomic cytoarchitecture reveals principles of human neocortex organization', dataset: 'Supercluster: IT-projecting excitatory neurons', Author Categories: 'CrossArea_subclass', L4 IT.\")\n35494:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.11165918\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4072039 \"The marker set RORB, ST8SIA4 can identify the Human cell type L4 intratelencephalic projecting glutamatergic neuron in the neocortex with a confidence of 0.720108696 (NS-Forest FBeta value).\")\n35503:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34004146\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1007/s00424-024-02923-2\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1101/2022.11.30.518285\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/c3aa4f95-7a18-4a7d-8dd8-ca324d714363.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072040 \"A transcriptomically distinct intratelencepalic-projecting glutamatergic neuron that expresses Car3 with a soma found in L6. The standard transcriptomic reference data for this cell type can be found on the CellxGene census under the collection: 'Transcriptomic cytoarchitecture reveals principles of human neocortex organization', dataset: 'Supercluster: IT-projecting excitatory neurons', Author Categories: 'CrossArea_cluster', L6 IT Car3.\")\n35512:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.11165918\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4072040 \"The marker set SMYD1, THEMIS can identify the Human cell type L6 intratelencephalic projecting Car3 glutamatergic neuron in the neocortex with a confidence of 0.877752028 (NS-Forest FBeta value).\")\n35521:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37292694\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37609206\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/c3aa4f95-7a18-4a7d-8dd8-ca324d714363.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072041 \"A transcriptomically distinct intratelencephalic-projecting glutamatergic neuron with a soma found in L6 of the primary motor cortex. These cells are short untufted pyramidal cells, which could be stellate or inverted.  The standard transcriptomic reference data for this cell type can be found on the CellxGene census under the collection: 'Transcriptomic cytoarchitecture reveals principles of human neocortex organization', dataset: 'Supercluster: IT-projecting excitatory neurons', Author Categories: 'CrossArea_subclass', L6 IT.\")\n35528:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.11165918\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4072041 \"The marker set LINC00507, THEMIS can identify the Human cell type L6 intratelencephalic projecting glutamatergic neuron in the neocortex with a confidence of 0.641695703 (NS-Forest FBeta value).\")\n35537:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34004146\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37292694\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/d01c9dff-abd1-4825-bf30-2eb2ba74597e.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072042 \"A transcriptomically defined near-projecting glutamatergic neuron with a soma found in cortical layer 5/6 in humans.\")\n35543:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.11165918\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4072042 \"The marker set NPSR1-AS1, TLL1 can identify the Human cell type L5/6 near-projecting glutamatergic neuron in the neocortex with a confidence of 0.899288218 (NS-Forest FBeta value).\")\n35552:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34616075\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/d01c9dff-abd1-4825-bf30-2eb2ba74597e.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072043 \"A transcriptomically distinct glutamatergic neuron, with a soma found in the deeper portion of L5, that has long-range axonal projections including deep subcortical targets outside of the telencephalon and, in some cases, the spinal cord. While the L5 ET neuron projections are not limited to ET targets, they are clearly differentiated from the neuron subclasses whose projections are constrained to intratelencephalic (IT) targets. L5 ET neurons are generally the largest excitatory cortical neurons, typically having a thick apical dendrite with a prominent dendritic tuft in layer 1 and displaying burst-firing physiological characteristics. The standard transcriptomic reference data for this cell type can be found on the CellxGene census under the collection: 'Transcriptomic cytoarchitecture reveals principles of human neocortex organization', dataset: 'Supercluster: Deep layer (non-IT) excitatory neurons ', Author Categories: 'CrossArea_subclass', clusters L5 ET.\")\n35564:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.11165918\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4072043 \"The marker set CHST8, POU3F1 can identify the Human cell type L5 extratelencephalic projecting glutamatergic cortical neuron in the neocortex with a confidence of 0.815891473 (NS-Forest FBeta value).\")\n35573:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34616075\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/d01c9dff-abd1-4825-bf30-2eb2ba74597e.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072044 \"A transcriptomically distinct corticothalamic-projecting neuron with a soma found in cortical layer 6. The standard transcriptomic reference data for this cell type can be found on the CellxGene census under the collection: 'Transcriptomic cytoarchitecture reveals principles of human neocortex organization', dataset: 'Supercluster: Deep layer (non-IT) excitatory neurons', Author Categories: 'CrossArea_subclass', clusters L6 CT.\")\n35580:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.11165918\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4072044 \"The marker set SEMA5B, ADAMTSL1, SULF1 can identify the Human cell type L6 corticothalamic-projecting glutamatergic cortical neuron in the neocortex with a confidence of 0.631898455 (NS-Forest FBeta value).\")\n35589:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.1101/2020.10.19.34312\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30382198\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/d01c9dff-abd1-4825-bf30-2eb2ba74597e.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072045 \"A glutamatergic neuron with a soma found in cortical layer 6b. They are transcriptomically related to corticothalamic-projecting neurons but have differential projections to the thalamus or anterior cingulate. The standard transcriptomic reference data for this cell type can be found on the CellxGene census under the collection: 'Transcriptomic cytoarchitecture reveals principles of human neocortex organization', dataset: 'Supercluster: Deep layer (non-IT) excitatory neuron', Author Categories: 'CrossArea_subclass', cluster L6b.\")\n35603:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27477017\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/9c63201d-bfd9-41a8-bbbc-18d947556f3d.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072046 \"A transcriptomically definined GABAergic interneuron of the human pallium.  These cells correspond to the classically defined pvalb chandelier neuron type. The standard transcriptomic reference data for this cell type can be found on the CellxGene census under the collection: 'Transcriptomic cytoarchitecture reveals principles of human neocortex organization', dataset: 'Supercluster: CGE-derived interneurons', Author Categories: 'CrossArea_subclass', clusters Chandelier.\")\n35612:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.11165918\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4072046 \"The marker set GPR149, CA8 can identify the Human cell type chandelier pvalb GABAergic cortical interneuron in the neocortex with a confidence of 0.799748111 (NS-Forest FBeta value).\")\n35671:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:license <http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35836364\") Annotation(rdfs:comment \"Trabecular meshwork (TM) structure. The TM consists of uveal (blue), corneoscleral (red), and juxtacanalicular (green) regions. TM beam cells (blue/red) line the uveal and corneoscleral regions, while JCT cells (green) occupy the juxtacanalicular region.\") foaf:depiction obo:CL_7770003 \"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/Trabecular_meshowk_cells_PMID35836364.jpg\")\n35688:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:license <http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35836364\") Annotation(rdfs:comment \"Trabecular meshwork (TM) structure. The TM consists of uveal (blue), corneoscleral (red), and juxtacanalicular (green) regions. TM beam cells (blue/red) line the uveal and corneoscleral regions, while JCT cells (green) occupy the juxtacanalicular region.\") foaf:depiction obo:CL_7770005 \"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/Trabecular_meshowk_cells_PMID35836364.jpg\")\n35699:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:license <http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35836364\") Annotation(rdfs:comment \"Trabecular meshwork (TM) structure. The TM consists of uveal (blue), corneoscleral (red), and juxtacanalicular (green) regions. TM beam cells (blue/red) line the uveal and corneoscleral regions, while JCT cells (green) occupy the juxtacanalicular region.\") foaf:depiction obo:CL_7770006 \"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/Trabecular_meshowk_cells_PMID35836364.jpg\")\n3