{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' PR_COMMENTS.md\"","aggregated_output":"## Summary\n\nUpdated `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl` for issue #3521 by adding Cell Annotation Platform reference transcriptomic dataset metadata to the 13 terms listed in the issue comment:\n\n- `CL_0000748`\n- `CL_0000751`\n- `CL_4033019`\n- `CL_4033027`\n- `CL_4033028`\n- `CL_4033029`\n- `CL_4033030`\n- `CL_4033031`\n- `CL_4033032`\n- `CL_4033033`\n- `CL_4033034`\n- `CL_4033035`\n- `CL_4033036`\n\nFor each listed term, I added:\n\n- a `term_tracker_item` annotation linking back to issue #3521,\n- a `database_cross_reference` to `https://celltype.info/project/544/dataset/1157`,\n- a labeled `rdfs:seeAlso` annotation for \"reference transcriptomic data on Cell Annotation Platform\",\n- definition text pointing to the CAP dataset `Single cell atlas of the human retina - Bipolar cell subclass - scRNA-seq`.\n\nFor specific cell types with a matching CAP `cell_type` label, the definition text also names the corresponding cluster. For `CL_0000748`, the wording refers to subclasses because the CAP dataset contains bipolar subclass labels rather than a direct `retinal bipolar neuron` label.\n\n## Rationale\n\nThe issue requested linkage to CAP dataset 1157 and definition text following the standard transcriptomic reference pattern. The CAP page describes the dataset as an integrated human retinal bipolar cell scRNA-seq atlas with `cell_type` labels for bipolar types, so the added metadata points terms to that reference dataset without changing their logical axioms or parentage.\n\nI did not add NS-Forest marker annotations in this change because the issue text says the linked CellMark PR still needs fixing and that CL mappings should drive automated inclusion once available.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Read imported issue title, body, and comments from `__issue_context__.json`.\n- [x] Checked existing term definitions and labels in `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl`.\n- [x] Checked existing ontology usage for `rdfs:seeAlso`, `database_cross_reference`, and `term_tracker_item`.\n- [x] Reviewed the CAP dataset page for dataset title and label-set context.\n- [x] Added CAP metadata and definition text for the 13 requested terms.\n- [x] Verified counts for issue tracker, CAP dbxref, and labeled `seeAlso` annotations: 13 each.\n- [x] Ran `git diff --check` successfully.\n- [ ] Ran `robot convert` validation: not completed because `robot` is not installed in this environment.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
